ingtel agreed to acquire the remaining 82% of STT GDC for S$6.6 billion, implying an enterprise value of about S$13.8 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8afcfdeb-2b04-4a83-8103-7473766336e4","evidence":"Global investment firm KKR, Asia’s leading communications technology group Singtel, and ST Telemedia today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR and Singtel (together, the “Consortium”) will acquire the remaining 82% stake in ST Telemedia Global Data Centres (“STT GDC” or the “Company”), a leading data centre colocation services provider, from founding shareholder ST Telemedia for a total consideration of S$6.6 billion (approximately US$5.1 billion). This represents an implied enterprise value of approximately S$13.8 billion (approximately US$10.9 billion), including leverage and capital expenditure for committed projects.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:b3ee355b34daf4e4de7bc900d502c71c","date":"2026-01-20","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Sylvan","portco_name":"Sylvan","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Novo Holdings"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR-led Consortium Drives Further Investment in Sylvan","summary":"KKR completed an additional investment in fungal biotechnology company Sylvan, with new investors and a follow-on from Novo Holdings; KKR remains majority investor.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=da4db7c1-661c-4b41-880d-fafcd187659a","evidence":"Global investment firm KKR today announced the completion of an additional investment in Sylvan, a world-leading fungal biotechnology company (the “Company”), through funds managed by KKR with participation from new investors and a follow-o