","target_website":"techone.nl","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Nedvest","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Techone Announces Strategic Partnership with KKR to further Accelerate Growth and Expand Market Position following Exit by Nedvest","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire Nedvest's majority stake in Dutch managed IT services provider Techone.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b4374e56-c22b-49a4-bb9c-20b1cbe654c7","evidence":"As part of the transaction, funds managed by KKR will acquire Nedvest’s majority stake in Techone.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f7fdf3f95ffe204b6eb800d6774bb8d1","date":"2025-11-16","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Chandra Asri Group","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Provides $750 Million Bespoke Financing Solution to Chandra Asri Group","summary":"KKR anchored a $750 million bespoke financing for Chandra Asri Group to support its acquisition of ExxonMobil's Esso fuel station network in Singapore.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9e299bbf-5060-4678-a902-593d876db613","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Chandra Asri Group (or the “Group”), a leading provider of energy, chemical, and infrastructure solutions in Southeast Asia, today announced a $750-million bespoke financing solution arranged by KKR Capital Markets and anchored by KKR’s private credit and insurance platforms to Chandra Asri Group. The investment will support the Group’s growth strategy and its acquisition of Esso-branded retail fuel station network from ExxonMobil in Singapore.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:780dd5fd51459adc10152846c0fe8ff1","date":"2025-11-10","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Novaria Group","portco_name":"Novaria Group","target_website":null,"investor":"Arcline Investment Management","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2200000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Arcline Investment Management to Acquire Novaria Group from KKR for $2.2 Billion","summary":"KKR agreed to sell aerospace components maker Novaria Group to Arcline in a transaction valued at $2.2 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=29dfcfab-52af-4f44-a83c-e8b9e47f12a3","evidence":"Leading investment firms KKR and Arcline Investment Management (“Arcline”) today announced that Arcline has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Novaria Group (“Novaria” or the “Company”), a leading provider of engineered aerospace components and specialty processes, in a transaction valued at $2.2 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:76e41c370ac5105cdadcfaf278b8f98e","date":"2025-10-27","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Keurig Dr Pepper","portco_name":"Keurig Dr Pepper","target_website":null,"investor":"Apollo","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":3000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Apollo Co-Lead $7B Strategic Investment in Keurig Dr Pepper","summary":"KKR and Apollo co-led a $3 billion convertible preferred stock investment in Keurig Dr Pepper, part of a $7 billion strategic investment package.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=44b108f8-4a11-433c-a483-725168d28419","evidence":"Investment: A definitive agreement for a $3 billion convertible preferred stock investment in the Company and the eventual Beverage Co., co-led by KKR and Apollo (the \"Preferred Investment\").","verified":true},{"key":"pr:5ad2810b1f98b1327b00b449e1c91ec1","date":"2025-10-27","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"KDP Pod Manufacturing JV","portco_name":"KDP Pod Manufacturing JV","target_website":null,"investor":"Apollo","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","Goldman Sachs Alternatives"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":4000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Apollo Co-Lead $7B Strategic Investment in Keurig Dr Pepper","summary":"Apollo and KKR co-led a $4 billion investment commitment in a new K-Cup pod manufacturing joint venture with Keurig Dr Pepper.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=44b108f8-4a11-433c-a483-725168d28419","evidence":"Pod Manufacturing JV: A binding commitment letter and term sheet for a $4 billion investment in a newly formed K-Cup® pod and other single-serve manufacturing joint venture (the \"Pod Manufacturing JV\") co-led by Apollo and KKR, with participation from Goldman Sachs Alternatives.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a5c93324b072466a66b391d21cd08aa4","date":"2025-10-20","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Peak Reinsurance Company Limited","portco_name":"Peak Reinsurance Company Limited","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Quadrantis Capital"],"seller":"Prudential Financial, Inc.","round":null,"stake_pct":11.27,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Peak Re Welcomes KKR and Quadrantis Capital as Minority Investors","summary":"KKR and Quadrantis Capital agreed to acquire minority stakes in Peak Re, with KKR expected to hold about 11.27%; Prudential divested its stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=94d1bdf9-69cb-4587-9d95-1da80b1c2abc","evidence":"Peak Reinsurance Company Limited (“Peak Re” or the “Company”) and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that funds managed by KKR and Quadrantis Capital have entered into definitive agreements to acquire minority stakes in Peak Re via Peak Reinsurance Holdings Limited. Upon completion, KKR and Quadrantis Capital are expected to hold approximately 11.27% and approximately 1.80% of Peak Re’s issued share capital, respectively, with the remaining approximately 86.71% continuing to be held by the majority shareholder, Fosun International Limited.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:a87bca352070cbd72c8369d8bf9ab5c7","date":"2025-10-20","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Galaxy Container Solutions","portco_name":"Galaxy Container Solutions","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Launches Galaxy Container Solutions, A Global Container Leasing and Financing Platform","summary":"KKR launched marine container leasing platform Galaxy Container Solutions with a $500 million commitment from its ABF strategy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a76f04ec-cae9-4a6d-bb1b-887309a88956","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the launch of Galaxy Container Solutions (“Galaxy” or “the Company”), a global marine container leasing and financing platform, in partnership with a team of industry veterans. Galaxy will be owned by KKR-managed credit funds and accounts, which are committing $500 million to the Company via KKR’s Asset-Based Finance (ABF) strategy.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:c10596a9dbb57ceef518d9c4b67b5925","date":"2025-10-14","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"BOND","portco_name":"BOND","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":320000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"BOND Launches Exclusive Aviation Club for the Premium Private Flyer with $350M Investment Led by KKR","summary":"Premium fractional aviation company BOND closed $320 million of preferred equity and debt financing led by KKR credit funds, plus $30 million equity from founding partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2993aec4-79bb-4ebb-9920-79988a6e8d5f","evidence":"NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--BOND, the world’s first premium fractional aviation company, today announced the close of $320 million in preferred equity and debt financing led by credit funds and accounts managed by leading global investment firm KKR, with $30 million of equity funding from a select group of founding partners.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:b49d599cc6455936e983e1892faaa907","date":"2025-10-01","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"ADNOC Gas Pipeline Assets LLC","portco_name":"ADNOC Gas Pipeline Assets","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"ADNOC","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Expands Strategic Partnership with ADNOC with Gas Pipelines Investment","summary":"KKR acquired a minority stake in ADNOC Gas Pipeline Assets through managed accounts.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=e1b719b5-1fd0-4bc4-86cc-e92f36fc2f1d","evidence":"Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates (UAE), 1 October, 2025 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that KKR has acquired a minority stake in ADNOC Gas Pipeline Assets LLC.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:d0877139f0cae26d38a681454b488824","date":"2025-09-29","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Infobric","portco_name":"Infobric Group","target_website":"infobric.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Infobric and Stirling Square Welcome KKR as New Investor","summary":"KKR made a growth investment in construction software provider Infobric, becoming a significant shareholder alongside majority owner Stirling Square.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ea7a0273-4083-4e99-b7d4-f5480b27520c","evidence":"Stirling Square Capital Partners (“Stirling Square”), a pan-European private equity firm, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announce that KKR is making a growth investment into Infobric (the “Company”), a leader in software solutions for the construction industry. KKR will become a significant shareholder alongside majority investor Stirling Square and Infobric’s management.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:2d24ed719a756f3add8e81c6aebc1e04","date":"2025-09-18","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Integrated Specialty Coverages","portco_name":"Integrated Specialty Coverages","target_website":null,"investor":"Onex Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Onex Partners to Acquire Integrated Specialty Coverages from KKR","summary":"KKR agreed to sell tech-enabled insurance platform ISC to Onex Partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=26945a43-5e28-4c26-8391-8866512e01fa","evidence":"NEW YORK, NY & CARLSBAD, CA September 18, 2025 – Leading global investment firms KKR and Onex today announced that Onex Partners will acquire Integrated Specialty Coverages (\"ISC\" or “the Company”), a tech-enabled insurance platform dedicated to designing, underwriting, and distributing insurance solutions.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f2b85d2de8523b437d5901e0e88d8e95","date":"2025-09-16","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Hoken Minaoshi Hompo Group, Inc.","portco_name":"Hoken Minaoshi Hompo","target_website":"mhompo.co.jp","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Advantage Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Japanese Insurance Distributor Hoken Minaoshi Hompo Group","summary":"KKR funds acquired Japanese insurance distributor Hoken Minaoshi Hompo Group from funds serviced by Advantage Partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1e96e710-b3d0-4cec-b972-d8ced1760d70","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that funds managed by KKR have acquired Hoken Minaoshi Hompo Group, Inc. (“Hoken Minaoshi Hompo Group”) from investment funds serviced by Advantage Partners (“AP”), a Japanese private equity sponsor.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7a0976bc68972d88f653a8d0ad35fc2c","date":"2025-09-04","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Samhwa Co., Ltd.","portco_name":"Samhwa","target_website":"e-samhwa.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"TPG","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Samhwa Secures Investment from KKR to Drive Next Chapter of Growth","summary":"KKR agreed to fully acquire Korean cosmetics packaging maker Samhwa from TPG at a valuation of KRW733 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=dd8a118f-6ed0-4c52-9a7a-a400efc6fe87","evidence":"Samhwa Co., Ltd. (“Samhwa” or the “Company”), a South Korean cosmetics packaging company, today announced the completion of an investment from funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm. KKR will fully acquire Samhwa from TPG at a valuation of KRW733 billion (~US$528 million).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b126008409d98dba06374e65994b147c","date":"2025-09-02","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Mirastar","portco_name":"Mirastar","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Increases Its Investment in Mirastar","summary":"KKR funds increased their investment in pan-European industrial and logistics platform Mirastar.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=e5542be9-e028-4b38-9188-13c5d4f191e5","evidence":"London – 2 September 2025 – After five years of successful strategic partnership, funds managed by KKR, a global investment firm, are increasing their investment in Mirastar to continue building on the success of its leading pan-European industrial and logistics platform.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:c132166c0196f6859179fca7d38d6d57","date":"2025-0