rved as lead investor on the debt financing for the recapitalization of Flexera Software (“Flexera” or the “Company”), a global leader in technology spend and risk intelligence. KKR Capital Markets also served as Lead Arranger and Bookrunner on the transaction.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5a00d81433591ebea64d012d6d25b618","date":"2025-08-14","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"CapeOmega Gas Transportation AS","portco_name":"CapeOmega","target_website":null,"investor":"Ocean Yield AS","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":"Partners Group","round":null,"stake_pct":100.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ocean Yield and KKR agree to acquire CapeOmega","summary":"KKR portfolio company Ocean Yield, with KKR vehicles, agreed to buy 100% of LNG carrier owner CapeOmega from Partners Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b9155938-d5ca-410b-a725-7c9e631c67e9","evidence":"Ocean Yield AS (\"Ocean Yield\" or the \"Company\") today announced that, together with vehicles managed by KKR (\"KKR\"), a leading global investment firm, it has agreed to purchase 100% of the shares in CapeOmega Gas Transportation AS (\"CapeOmega\") from Partners Group, acting on behalf of its clients.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:75ae6e97fe01d5b1c898c070d5f94c39","date":"2025-08-14","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Headlands Research","portco_name":"Headlands Research","target_website":null,"investor":"THL Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"THL Announces Agreement to Acquire Headlands Research from KKR","summary":"THL agreed to acquire clinical trial site network Headlands Research from KKR funds.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2458bd89-5518-44f6-ab32-d338cf4cb754","evidence":"LAKE WORTH, Fla. & NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--THL Partners (“THL”), a premier private equity firm investing in middle market growth companies, today announced the entry into a definitive agreement to acquire Headlands Research (“Headlands” or “the Company”), a leading multinational network of clinical trial sites, from funds managed by leading global investment firm KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:6016aac6c974ffa819d80ecc4a5f0207","date":"2025-08-08","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Med-Metrix, LLC","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Leads Financing for Harvest Partners’ Growth Investment in Med-Metrix","summary":"KKR credit funds led the financing supporting Harvest Partners' growth investment in revenue cycle management provider Med-Metrix.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=93576b7c-1ff2-4236-a067-c275b98edda6","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that credit funds and accounts managed by KKR served as lead investors on a financing to support the growth investment from funds managed by Harvest Partners, LP (“Harvest”) in Med-Metrix, LLC (“Med-Metrix” or “the Company”), a leading provider of technology-enabled Revenue Cycle Management (\"RCM\") solutions.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:84072a16db07a1eff85dc2540e55f755","date":"2025-08-06","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"DentalXChange","portco_name":"DentalXChange","target_website":"dentalxchange.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Bregal Sagemount","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"DentalXChange Announces Recapitalization with KKR to Advance Technology and Innovation in Dental Revenue Cycle Management","summary":"KKR led the recapitalization of dental revenue cycle management provider DentalXChange, with Bregal Sagemount exiting its investment.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a38bbee0-d5ec-47ea-b461-bc58cf9ebf21","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the recapitalization of DentalXChange (“DXC” or the “Company”), a leading provider of revenue cycle management (RCM) solutions for the U.S. dental market. In connection with the transaction, Bregal Sagemount exited its investment in DXC, following a successful strategic partnership with the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:08191e597b303f5aef7f49435f7277fd","date":"2025-07-30","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"HealthCare Royalty Partners","portco_name":"HealthCare Royalty Partners","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Strategic Acquisition of HealthCare Royalty Partners, Expanding the Firm’s Health Care Franchise and Enhancing its Life Sciences Strategy","summary":"KKR & Co. acquired a majority ownership stake in biopharma royalty acquisition company HealthCare Royalty Partners (HCRx).","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9a3c81b1-b97f-470f-852b-0c4068f56928","evidence":"KKR & Co. Inc., a leading global investment firm, today announced that it has acquired a majority ownership stake in HealthCare Royalty Partners (HCRx), a leading biopharma royalty acquisition company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:07b9ca2b72c27b64f00829a1f84dfafb","date":"2025-07-30","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Harley-Davidson Financial Services","portco_name":"Harley-Davidson Financial Services","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["PIMCO"],"seller":"Harley-Davidson","round":null,"stake_pct":4.9,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Harley-Davidson Announces Strategic Partnership with KKR and PIMCO","summary":"KKR and PIMCO each agreed to buy a 4.9% common equity interest in Harley-Davidson Financial Services alongside purchases of more than $5 billion of its retail loan receivables.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=6f392966-236d-4164-83cc-6694b9e8b411","evidence":"Transaction monetizes HDFS through sale of 4.9% common equity interests to each partner and includes the sale of more than $5 billion of retail loan receivables at a premium to par","verified":null},{"key":"pr:df1ebf2fe2e19d87d80eb417463009bf","date":"2025-07-21","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Etraveli Group","portco_name":"Etraveli Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC welcomes strategic minority partnership investment from KKR into Etraveli Group","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a significant minority stake in CVC-backed travel technology company Etraveli Group; financial details were not disclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c582c5aa-bd96-49b6-b93c-c08dd1e5c2e4","evidence":"CVC Capital Partners (“CVC”) today announced that KKR has agreed to acquire a significant minority stake in global travel technology company Etraveli Group. Financial details of the transaction have not been disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:20da868e6f4550f2a7c1ea922924ccf4","date":"2025-07-17","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"SupplyHouse","portco_name":"SupplyHouse","target_website":"supplyhouse.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"SupplyHouse Receives Strategic Investment from KKR","summary":"KKR-affiliated funds invested in HVAC, plumbing and electrical e-commerce distributor SupplyHouse as a strategic partner.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f2fd83d6-dfe0-4aa8-90d6-1be6e052213e","evidence":"Melville, NY and New York, NY – July 17, 2025 – SupplyHouse (or, the “Company”), a leading pure-play e-commerce platform for the distribution of HVAC, plumbing, and electrical products, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced the formation of a strategic partnership to support the Company’s long-term growth strategy. As part of the strategic partnership, funds affiliated with KKR have invested in SupplyHouse.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:76e43e81ebb8ee602162b83a7be34f09","date":"2025-07-16","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"ghSMART","portco_name":"ghSMART","target_website":"ghsmart.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Leadership Advisory Firm ghSMART Announces Significant Minority Investment from KKR","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire a significant minority stake in leadership advisory firm ghSMART; terms were not disclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f59762a5-3cfb-48b3-b950-6e9d6f6107db","evidence":"NEW YORK, July 16, 2025—ghSMART, a premier global leadership advisory firm, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that funds managed by KKR will acquire a significant minority stake in ghSMART (the “Company”). ghSMART partners with CEOs, boards, and investors to develop effective executive teams and support high-stakes leadership decisions. ghSMART’s founder, partners, and employees will retain majority ownership in the business and the current management team, led by CEO Jeff McLean, will continue to lead the company in their current roles. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:6eec20d9126d4dfe260fb27ca865eb49","date":"2025-07-14","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Perrigo Dermacosmetics business","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Kairos Bidco AB","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":"Perrigo Company plc","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":327000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Perrigo Announces Agreement to Divest Dermacosmetics Business for up to €327 Million","summary":"A KKR-managed vehicle agreed to buy Perrigo's Dermacosmetics branded business for up to €327 million, including €300 million upfront.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=154fdc98-caec-4505-94fe-90e15037bc64","evidence":"Dublin, Ireland – July 14, 2025 – Perrigo Company plc (NYSE: PRGO) (“Perrigo” or the “Company”), a leading global provider of Consumer Self-Care Products, today announced it has signed an agreement with Kairos Bidco AB, an investment vehicle managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, to sell the Company’s Dermacosmetics branded business for up to €327 million, including €300 million in upfront cash and up to an additional €27 million contingent on the achievement of net sales milestones over the next three years.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:e8820a64f2e039908f12caad698711fd","date":"2025-07-27","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"CleanPeak Energy","portco_name":"CleanPeak Energy","target_website":"cleanpeakenergy.com.au","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"AUD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Forms A$500 Million Strategic Partnership with CleanPeak Energy to Launch New Distributed Energy Platform","summary":"KKR funds agreed to commit A$500 million to partner with Australian distributed energy platform CleanPeak Energy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a09e8b5f-634c-42f4-a166-fd6768116cb8","evidence":"Global investment firm KKR today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will commit A$500 million to strategically partner with CleanPeak Energy (“CleanPeak”) to rapidly grow its distributed energy platform.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:aa366fec341055272e39734ee91e57b7","date":"2025-07-01","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"ProTen Pty Limited","portco_name":"ProTen","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Aware Super","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires ProTen from Aware Super","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire Australian poultry farm infrastructure business ProTen from Aware Super.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=39086956-e5fd-44c8-9d87-49a4820138cf","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Aware Super, a leading Australian super fund, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will acquire ProTen Pty Limited (“ProTen”), one of the largest agricultural infrastructure businesses in Australia, from Aware Super.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b02da6fe7f2f854f832af60ecfa37878","date":"2025-06-30","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ascend Asia Financial Services Group","portco_name":"Ascend Asia","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Launches Financial Advisory Platform Ascend Asia in Singapore","summary":"KKR launched Singapore financial advisory platform Ascend Asia, led by former Prudential Singapore CEO Tomas Urbanec.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b58fb795-b73b-4b68-82f3-03ecca11b73a","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the launch of Ascend Asia Financial Services Group (“Ascend Asia”), a newly established financial advisory platform in Singapore.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:2510a5d656798bf75276995e3371b519","date":"2025-06-30","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"finexis","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Ascend Asia Financial Services Group","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Launches Financial Advisory Platform Ascend Asia in Singapore","summary":"KKR-backed Ascend Asia agreed to acquire Singapore financial advisory firm finexis as its first member firm.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b58fb795-b73b-4b68-82f3-03ecca11b73a","evidence":"Concurrently, Ascend Asia, through funds managed by KKR, has entered into definitive agreements to acquire finexis advisory and its affiliates (together, “finexis”), marking finexis as the platform’s inaugural member firm.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:3fbcb593d18e62b8bae5befa0738e245","date":"2025-06-29","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals","portco_name":"J.B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals","target_website":null,"investor":"Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":46.39,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Torrent Pharma to Acquire Controlling Stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals from KKR","summary":"Torrent Pharma agreed to acquire a controlling stake in JB Pharma from KKR at an equity valuation of INR 25,689 crores, buying 46.39% for INR 11,917 crores.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d074105a-2376-41bd-807e-c2cf155f111d","evidence":"Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited (“Torrent”) and global investment firm KKR today announced that Torrent has entered into definitive agreements to acquire controlling stake in J. B. Chemicals and Pharmaceuticals (“JB Pharma”) from KKR at an Equity Valuation of INR 25,689 crores (on fully diluted basis), followed by a merger of the two entities. Acquisition of 46.39% equity stake (on a fully diluted basis) through a Share Purchase Agreement (“SPA”) at a consideration of INR 11,917 crores (INR 1,600 per share) followed by a mandatory open offer to acquire up to 26% of JB Pharma shares from public shareholders at an open offer price of INR 1,639.18 per share.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:742825e617d295c9506bf019e6f1d069","date":"2025-06-16","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Zenith Energy","portco_name":"Zenith Energy","target_website":"zenithenergy.com.au","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Pacific Equity Partners, OPSEU Pension Trust, Foresight Group","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Leading Australian Independent Power Producer Zenith Energy","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Australian independent power producer Zenith Energy from a consortium of PEP, OPTrust and Foresight Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f604b966-5b05-4051-83f4-0bf0bb2f0b8a","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of definitive agreements to acquire Zenith Energy (“Zenith” or the “Company”), a leading independent power producer (“IPP”), from a consortium including Pacific Equity Partners, OPSEU Pension Trust (“OPTrust”), and Foresight Group (together the “Consortium”), with Zenith’s founder and management retaining a minority stake.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:0f210510e6e4eac762b5275ef674c4c8","date":"2025-06-08","date_text":null,"kind":"secondary","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Pinnacle Towers","portco_name":"Pinnacle Towers Pte Ltd","target_website":"frontiertowersphilippines.com","investor":"BCI","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"BCI Invests in KKR Tower Platform Pinnacle Towers","summary":"British Columbia Investment Management Corporation agreed to acquire a minority stake in Philippine tower platform Pinnacle Towers from KKR, which remains majority owner.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b9eb115a-0e71-4618-b91b-1b71f6c817ec","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, British Columbia Investment Management Corporation (“BCI”), and Pinnacle Towers, an Asia-based digital infrastructure platform with a focus on the Philippines, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which BCI will acquire a minority stake in Pinnacle Towers from KKR, which will remain the majority shareholder.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:8c4763005043e2f7b32bd22e7a67fc78","date":"2025-06-09","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"HarbourView Equity Partners","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"HarbourView Closes on $500 Million in Additional Debt Financing from KKR","summary":"HarbourView closed $500 million of additional debt financing through a private securitization in which KKR-managed insurance vehicles participated.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=35b6e517-f1d5-4ccb-84fc-d83f00a54878","evidence":"NEWARK, N.J., June 9, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- HarbourView Equity Partners (HarbourView), an alternative asset management company focused on investment opportunities in the entertainment, media, and sports space, with approximately *$2.67B in regulatory assets under management, has closed an additional $500 million in debt financing through a new private securitization backed by its diversified, scaled music portfolio. Insurance vehicles managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, participated in the transaction.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:e7956ff73a3b707a52c4df7767241ddb","date":"2025-03-28","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Topcon Corporation","portco_name":"Topcon Corporation","target_website":"global.topcon.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["JIC Capital"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Topcon to Accelerate Growth through Management Buyout with KKR and JIC Capital","summary":"Topcon launched a management buyout backed by KKR funds and JIC Capital via a tender offer at JPY 3,300 per share.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=80719d0b-3c53-4a8f-91f8-9a983b9e382f","evidence":"TOKYO, Japan – March 28, 2025 – Topcon Corporation (“Topcon” or the “Company”; TSE stock code 7732), today announced that it is launching a management buyout (“MBO”) led by Topcon President and CEO Takashi Eto. The MBO will receive investment from funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, and JIC Capital (“JICC”), a wholly owned subsidiary of Japan Investment Corporation (“JIC”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:64e70a1377bb14cda6f111d9cbe5b39c","date":"2025-02-05","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"XOi","portco_name":"Xoi","target_website":"xoi.io","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"XOi Amplifies Field Service Innovation with New Strategic Investment and Acquisition","summary":"Field service technology company XOi received its largest funding to date from KKR funds, which enabled its acquisition of Specifx.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5f054a8f-e637-4196-919d-55843711f4e5","evidence":"The acquisition was enabled by an investment from funds managed by leading global investment firm KKR. The funding from KKR marks the most significant milestone yet in XOi’s journey to build out its system of work for the field service ecosystem.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:331c1911b3abd8df71c10500a654bb0a","date":"2025-02-05","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Specifx","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"XOi","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"XOi Amplifies Field Service Innovation with New Strategic Investment and Acquisition","summary":"KKR-backed XOi acquired field service equipment data enrichment platform Specifx.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5f054a8f-e637-4196-919d-55843711f4e5","evidence":"NASHVILLE, Tenn.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--XOi, a leading provider of jobsite-focused technology solutions for the field service ecosystem, today announced the acquisition of Specifx, an on-demand data enrichment and metadata retrieval platform for field service equipment. The acquisition was enabled by an investment from funds managed by leading global investment firm KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1c32e5f2bb95a641f8d74b1a21742873","date":"2025-01-29","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Henry Schein","portco_name":"Henry Schein","target_website":"henryschein.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":12.0,"amount":250000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Henry Schein Announce Strategic Investment","summary":"KKR agreed to invest an additional $250 million in Henry Schein common stock, taking its position to 12%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d55b21b8-18be-43b4-8ae0-62a545d48894","evidence":"In addition to KKR’s current holdings, KKR will make an additional $250 million investment in the Company’s common stock (the “Investment”). As a result, KKR will become the largest non-index fund shareholder in the Company with a 12% position, demonstrating the firm’s confidence in Henry Schein, its management team, and its BOLD+1 strategy.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:343b712cec096ef614c17db38a2c310c","date":"2025-01-21","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Dawsongroup","portco_name":"Dawsongroup","target_website":"dawsongroup.co.uk","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Dawsongroup to Accelerate Growth and Support Fleet Transition","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire UK asset leasing business Dawsongroup from its shareholders through its Global Climate strategy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=07025cbe-5dec-48cb-ba79-3887e2fa4337","evidence":"Dawsongroup (the ”Group”), a leading independent asset leasing business which provides a diverse range of business-critical solutions, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announce that KKR has entered into a binding agreement with the shareholders of Dawsongroup to acquire the Group.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7a2c299fe1fafe23457984328559a58c","date":"2025-01-17","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Gulf Data Hub","portco_name":"Gulf Data Hub","target_website":"gulfdatahub.ae","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Gulf Data Hub Form Strategic Partnership to Scale One of the Middle East’s Largest Independent Data Center Platforms","summary":"KKR-affiliated funds agreed to acquire a stake in Middle East data center platform Gulf Data Hub, with the partners committing to support over $5 billion of total investment.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=7a64b850-b2ae-4747-bc71-5d58b8e82f50","evidence":"Gulf Data Hub (“GDH” or the “Company”), one of the largest independent data center platforms in the Middle East focused on serving hyperscale demand across the Gulf countries, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that funds affiliated with KKR will acquire a stake in GDH.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:35efa5cdbc77f9a2463beb5041369b08","date":"2025-01-16","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"smaXtec","portco_name":"smaXtec","target_website":"smaxtec.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Highland Europe"],"seller":null,"round":"growth","stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in smaXtec to Accelerate Global Growth","summary":"KKR led a growth investment in dairy agri-tech provider smaXtec alongside Highland Europe; Sophora retained a minority stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=851533ea-ec9e-4be2-9598-7278197e54ad","evidence":"London, UK & Graz, Austria – 16 January 2025 – smaXtec, a leading provider of agri-tech for the global dairy industry, today announced a growth investment led by global investment firm, KKR, alongside technology investor Highland Europe (“Highland”). Existing shareholder Sophora Unternehmerkapital (“Sophora”) retained a minority stake in the business.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:514ab2a9a77f4706ae4b85545b76591a","date":"2025-01-13","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Qventus Inc","portco_name":"Qventus Inc","target_website":"qventus.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Bessemer Venture Partners","Northwestern Medicine","HonorHealth","Allina Health"],"seller":null,"round":"Series D","stake_pct":null,"amount":105000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Qventus Announces $105 Million Investment, Series D Led by KKR","summary":"Qventus raised a $105 million Series D led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1212261d-299a-4108-aff0-d9a52f8ead2b","evidence":"NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Qventus, a leading provider of AI-based care automation software for health systems, today announced a $105 million investment led by global investment firm KKR, with additional participation from world-renowned investment firm Bessemer Venture Partners, and new strategic investors, including leading health systems Northwestern Medicine, HonorHealth, and Allina Health.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:02741d8e7b986672d9e549615b3d2b4d","date":"2025-01-09","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"AEP Ohio and Indiana Michigan transmission companies","portco_name":"AEP Ohio and Indiana Michigan transmission companies","target_website":"aeptransmission.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["PSP Investments"],"seller":"American Electric Power","round":null,"stake_pct":19.9,"amount":2820000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and PSP Investments Acquire Minority Stake in Two American Electric Power Transmission Companies","summary":"KKR and PSP Investments agreed to acquire a 19.9% interest in AEP's Ohio and Indiana Michigan transmission companies for $2.82 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=641d2d40-1748-4915-b0ae-9b20c602cd01","evidence":"Today, investment funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, and the Public Sector Pension Investment Board (“PSP Investments”), one of Canada’s largest pension investors, announced an agreement to acquire a 19.9% interest in American Electric Power’s (“AEP”) Ohio and Indiana & Michigan transmission companies for $2.82 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0df99d53c5eb598ac9dadee2b7896de9","date":"2024-12-19","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Rebel Foods","portco_name":"Rebel Foods","target_website":"rebelfoods.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Leading Internet Restaurant Company Rebel Foods","summary":"KKR affiliates completed an investment in Indian internet restaurant company Rebel Foods.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=edd017c7-14d4-437f-b99b-8786cba1a227","evidence":"Rebel Foods, a leading internet restaurant company, and global investment firm KKR today announced the completion of an investment in Rebel Foods by affiliates of KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:e971d3bf37f9f9044678870e33d32d00","date":"2024-12-19","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"The Stepstone Group","portco_name":"The Stepstone Group","target_website":"thestepstonegroup.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["CPP Investments"],"seller":"Axel Springer SE","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Axel Springer Announces Signing of Definitive Agreement on New Corporate Structure to Unlock Future Growth Potential","summary":"Under Axel Springer's restructuring, Stepstone becomes a separate joint venture company majority-owned by KKR and CPP Investments, with Axel Springer keeping about 10%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c88cf4ce-3d76-47d8-90e1-15d00d712f2d","evidence":"The classifieds businesses - the Stepstone Group and AVIV Group – will be held as separate joint venture companies with KKR and CPP Investments as majority shareholders, Axel Springer as minority co-shareholder (approximately 10 percent), and with an economic participation by the grandchildren of Axel Springer.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ebfbf3bbd1dc3e1bfd02ca73b2a4f436","date":"2024-12-19","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"AVIV Group","portco_name":"AVIV Group","target_website":"aviv-group.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["CPP Investments"],"seller":"Axel Springer SE","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Axel Springer Announces Signing of Definitive Agreement on New Corporate Structure to Unlock Future Growth Potential","summary":"Under Axel Springer's restructuring, AVIV Group becomes a separate joint venture company majority-owned by KKR and CPP Investments.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c88cf4ce-3d76-47d8-90e1-15d00d712f2d","evidence":"The classifieds businesses - the Stepstone Group and AVIV Group – will be held as separate joint venture companies with KKR and CPP Investments as majority shareholders, Axel Springer as minority co-shareholder (approximately 10 percent), and with an economic participation by the grandchildren of Axel Springer.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f2bb862b0ac6f7e570f0bbb8a16f3ce5","date":"2024-12-19","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Aiwyn Inc","portco_name":"Aiwyn Inc","target_website":"aiwyn.ai","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Bessemer Venture Partners"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":113000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Aiwyn Secures $113M in Funding from KKR and Bessemer Venture Partners to Revolutionize Firm Operations and Tax Technology for Leading CPA Firms","summary":"Accounting technology firm Aiwyn closed a $113 million funding round led by KKR and Bessemer Venture Partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=934b80c4-2263-4857-ab47-7464cf334a6a","evidence":"CHARLOTTE, N.C.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Aiwyn, a trusted technology partner for top Certified Public Accounting (“CPA”) firms, today announced the successful close of a $113M funding round. This landmark investment, led by leading global investment firm KKR and Bessemer Venture Partners underscores Aiwyn’s leadership in the accounting technology sector.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a392b5d65384445ae922da5f18babeed","date":"2024-12-19","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"The Citation Group","portco_name":"Citation Group","target_website":"thecitationgroup.com","investor":"HarbourVest Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Citation welcomes new investment from HarbourVest Partners supporting its growth as a global provider of SME compliance and certification solutions","summary":"HarbourVest Partners invested in Citation alongside existing backers Hg and KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=02f75285-97ff-45af-ae8a-98ddb4a6fb04","evidence":"HarbourVest Partners joins forces with Hg and KKR to propel Citation's growth ambitions, international expansion and innovation in AI. London, UK – 19 December, 2024 – The Citation Group (Citation), an international provider of tech-enabled compliance and certification solutions to small to medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), today announce that they have welcomed HarbourVest Partners (HarbourVest), a global private markets investment manager, as a new investor in the business.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1d19fb019a2959d0e37559d3e5355b75","date":"2025-03-31","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"ReliaQuest LLC","portco_name":"ReliaQuest LLC","target_website":"reliaquest.com","investor":"EQT","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","FTV Capital","Ten Eleven Ventures","Finback Investment Partners"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":3400000000.0,"valuation_currency":"USD","headline":"ReliaQuest Raises More Than $500 Million in Funding at a Valuation of $3.4 Billion","summary":"ReliaQuest raised more than $500 million led by EQT, KKR and FTV Capital at a $3.4 billion valuation.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=10051b1a-d672-44fb-887d-ce2ae3ee904a","evidence":"TAMPA, Fla. & NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--ReliaQuest, a leader in AI-powered security operations, today announced a new funding round of more than $500 million led by EQT, KKR and FTV Capital, with participation from other existing investors Ten Eleven Ventures and Finback Investment Partners. The funding round brings ReliaQuest’s valuation to $3.4 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:90395723355c92839b435a049b13bd46","date":"2025-03-05","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Darwinbox","portco_name":"Darwinbox","target_website":"darwinbox.com","investor":"Partners Group","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","Gravity Holdings"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":140000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Darwinbox Raises $140 Million Investment Co-led by Partners Group and KKR to Accelerate Global Expansion","summary":"HR technology platform Darwinbox raised $140 million co-led by Partners Group and KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4270d54e-83c6-47a3-93b3-e3795de06f6c","evidence":"Darwinbox, a leading global human resource (“HR”) technology platform, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which Partners Group, one of the largest firms in the global private markets industry (acting on behalf of its clients), and funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, will co-lead an investment of $140 million in the company, with additional participation from Gravity Holdings.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:4916372c42249366a99c67ede8e3438a","date":"2025-03-05","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Seiyu","portco_name":"Seiyu","target_website":null,"investor":"Trial Holdings, Inc.","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR, Walmart","round":null,"stake_pct":85.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Sell Seiyu to Trial Holdings","summary":"KKR agreed to sell its 85% stake in Japanese supermarket chain Seiyu to Trial Holdings, with Walmart also selling its 15%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2b73433f-5042-46b5-a914-730f65a55835","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Seiyu, a nationwide supermarket chain in Japan, today announced the signing of definitive agreements to sell Seiyu (the “Company”) to Trial Holdings, Inc. (TSE stock code 141A; “Trial”), a distribution and retail business operator in Japan that operates a network of stores offering “everyday essentials” in Kyushu. KKR first acquired a 65% majority stake in Seiyu from Walmart in 2021, before acquiring an additional 20% stake from Rakuten in 2023, taking KKR’s shareholding to 85%. As part of the transaction, Walmart will also sell its 15% stake to Trial.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5d53c44cd29452f95845510c06a27ade","date":"2025-03-04","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"FlowMod","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Ajax Health","Boston Scientific Corporation"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ajax Health and KKR Form New Platform to Develop System for Treating Heart Failure","summary":"KKR-backed Ajax Health formed heart failure device company FlowMod with Boston Scientific IP, funded through KKR Health Care Strategic Growth Fund II.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f4422dc0-690f-4a15-8e5d-e248e0570021","evidence":"MENLO PARK, Calif., March 4, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- Ajax Health, a KKR-backed medical device platform, today announced the formation of a new entity, FlowMod. The new organization is the result of a collaboration between Boston Scientific Corporation, Ajax Health, and KKR, utilizing intellectual property developed by Boston Scientific. KKR is investing in FlowMod through its KKR Health Care Strategic Growth Fund II, a $4.0 billion fund focused on investing in high-growth health care companies.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5958a56f7e9d9a6a57ecbf4b83102001","date":"2025-03-02","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Family Doctor Pty Ltd.","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Provides Bespoke Financing Solution to Australian GP Group Family Doctor","summary":"KKR funds provided a bespoke financing solution to Australian GP clinic group Family Doctor.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=e51fd332-b71b-4866-95a8-bf9ec51e392e","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Family Doctor Pty Ltd. (“Family Doctor”), a leading group of general practitioner (“GP”) clinics in Australia, today announced a bespoke financing solution by KKR (through funds managed by KKR) to Family Doctor. KKR’s bespoke financing solution positions the Family Doctor to accelerate its growth and expansion, including through acquisitions.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:8ebf54537ad1d1f9b976700cfbb5386d","date":"2025-02-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"HealthCare Global Enterprises","portco_name":"HealthCare Global Enterprises","target_website":"hcgoncology.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"CVC","round":null,"stake_pct":54.0,"amount":400000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Controlling Stake in Indian Healthcare Provider Healthcare Global Enterprises for $400 Million","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire up to 54% of Indian cancer care provider HCG from CVC at INR 445 per share, becoming controlling shareholder in a deal the headline sizes at $400 million.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a2314ae6-b43c-44db-8812-a4f3c8329b2f","evidence":"KKR Acquires Controlling Stake in Indian Healthcare Provider Healthcare Global Enterprises for $400 Million KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Healthcare Global Enterprises (BSE: 539787; NSE: HCG; “HCG”), a leading healthcare organization in India, today announced the signing of definitive agreements with CVC, a leading global private markets manager, under which funds managed by KKR (“KKR”) will become the largest shareholder in HCG and assume sole control of HCG’s operations. As part of the transaction, KKR will acquire up to 54% of equity in HCG from CVC Asia V at a purchase price of INR 445 per share.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:95207a29c22884d1a11afe8d43bf6789","date":"2025-02-18","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"EGC","portco_name":"EGC","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Enters Into Strategic Partnership With Energy Service Provider EGC","summary":"KKR signed agreements for a strategic partnership with Düsseldorf energy service provider EGC, with the founding family retaining a stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ef21a6ee-881b-41f5-b12b-ad3bc9d70922","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced that KKR has signed agreements to enter into a strategic partnership with EGC, an energy service provider based in Düsseldorf, Germany. The founding family and current shareholders will retain a stake in the company and will remain active members of the management team.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:cd65ca5609e6d5bfab58361b4a88ee28","date":"2025-02-17","date_text":null,"kind":"secondary","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Employment Hero","portco_name":"Employment Hero","target_website":"employmenthero.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"SEEK Investments","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Stake in HRM Platform Employment Hero from SEEK Investments","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire a stake in HR platform Employment Hero from SEEK Investments.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=56c551a1-fa3d-49d7-bf46-27cefb39da34","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, Employment Hero, a global leader in employment management solutions, and SEEK Investments, manager of the SEEK Growth Fund, a long-term investment fund focused on human capital management, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will acquire a stake in Employment Hero (“the Company”) from SEEK Investments.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:14a64f9a5cb78cbf3dd02de6a192276e","date":"2025-02-10","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Kito Crosby Limited","portco_name":"Kito Crosby","target_website":null,"investor":"Columbus McKinnon Corporation","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2700000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Columbus McKinnon to Combine with Kito Crosby Delivering Compelling Value Creation","summary":"Columbus McKinnon agreed to acquire lifting solutions maker Kito Crosby from KKR funds in an all-cash transaction valued at $2.7 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5af6165b-acd9-47d8-b6a7-a7c9859d3697","evidence":"CHARLOTTE, NC, February 10, 2025 - Columbus McKinnon Corporation (Nasdaq: CMCO) (\"Columbus McKinnon\" or the \"Company\"), a leading designer, manufacturer and marketer of intelligent motion solutions for material handling, today announced a definitive agreement under which Columbus McKinnon will acquire Kito Crosby Limited (“Kito Crosby”) from funds managed by leading global investment firm KKR in an all-cash transaction valued at $2.7 billion subject to customary post-closing purchase price adjustments.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:febb6b21857a0d5d4cda74e62b410ef3","date":"2025-06-02","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Manipal Education and Medical Group","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Provides $600 Million Financing to Indian Conglomerate Manipal Group","summary":"KKR anchored a $600 million financing arranged by KKR Capital Markets for Indian conglomerate Manipal Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=189eb5b7-b32e-417a-b05a-2c5f93f3f46e","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Manipal Education and Medical Group (“MEMG” or “Manipal Group”), a major diversified conglomerate in India, today announced a $600-million financing arranged by KKR Capital Markets and anchored by KKR’s private credit and insurance platforms to the Manipal Group.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ffffe8d4c340dd7604872789b646f093","date":"2025-05-22","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"West Star Aviation","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Leads Financing for Greenbriar’s Acquisition of West Star Aviation","summary":"KKR credit funds led the debt financing for Greenbriar Equity Group's acquisition of West Star Aviation.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=774fd3a7-0ff7-49dd-962f-3135353fffd0","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that credit funds and accounts managed by KKR served as lead investors on a debt financing for Greenbriar Equity Group's acquisition of West Star Aviation (“West Star” or the “Company”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:02be2a0be272ecf3760528f6fc0d5b48","date":"2025-04-14","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Osttra Group Ltd","portco_name":"Osttra Group Ltd","target_website":"osttra.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"CME Group, S&P Global","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":3100000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire OSTTRA from CME Group and S&P Global for $3.1 Billion","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire post-trade solutions provider OSTTRA from CME Group and S&P Global at a total enterprise value of $3.1 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=fe358680-3d41-40c1-b24e-5b88a32b061a","evidence":"New York, NY, April 14, 2025— KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of a definitive agreement under which investment funds managed by KKR will acquire OSTTRA, a leading provider of post-trade solutions for the global OTC market, from CME Group and S&P Global. The terms of the deal for OSTTRA equaled total enterprise value at $3.1 billion, subject to customary purchase price adjustments, which will be divided evenly between S&P Global and CME Group pursuant to their 50/50 joint venture.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:91ad0cf9514df2da8721ca89dc0c3ad6","date":"2025-04-02","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Sylvan","portco_name":"Sylvan","target_website":null,"investor":"Novo Holdings","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Sylvan Receives Investment from Novo Holdings to Drive Further Growth","summary":"Novo Holdings agreed to make a direct investment in KKR-backed fungal biotechnology company Sylvan; KKR remains majority shareholder.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8e2f1fcd-4463-4650-8401-6565749db664","evidence":"Novo Holdings, a leading global life science investor, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which Novo Holdings will make a direct investment in Sylvan, a world-leading manufacturer of fungal biotechnology solutions (or the “Company”). KKR will remain the Company’s majority shareholder.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4b3c1c8c0b14cac2abcc34b5ed447f5c","date":"2024-11-21","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Lighthouse","portco_name":"Lighthouse","target_website":"mylighthouse.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Spectrum Equity","F-Prime Capital","Eight Roads Ventures","Highgate Technology Ventures"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":370000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Lighthouse Announces $370 Million Series C Investment Led by KKR to Accelerate Platform Innovation and Growth","summary":"Hospitality commercial intelligence platform Lighthouse announced an approximately $370 million Series C growth investment led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=16dbd46d-d91f-4f54-b8c5-0bd4d83daeac","evidence":"Lighthouse, the leading commercial intelligence platform for the travel & hospitality industry, today announced an approximately $370 million growth investment led by global investment firm, KKR. Existing investors Spectrum Equity, F-Prime Capital, Eight Roads Ventures, and Highgate Technology Ventures will continue their participation in the business.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8b8c933b1471cec20e638e3cc7c83147","date":"2024-11-12","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"24SevenOffice ERP software division","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Accountor Software","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":"24SevenOffice","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Accountor Software combines with 24SevenOffice’s ERP software division to expand Nordic footprint","summary":"KKR-backed Accountor Software agreed to acquire 24SevenOffice's ERP software division to expand in the Nordics.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=901ba996-b9de-409e-8cf9-6536f0f28c05","evidence":"Accountor Software and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announce the next phase of Accountor Software’s growth journey; the acquisition of 24SevenOffice’s ERP software division, comprising among others 24SevenOffice Norway AS, 24SevenOffice Scandinavia Systems AS, and 24SevenOffice Sweden AB.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:09b2711d055012b00a6737a9910dddeb","date":"2024-11-04","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"eRESI Capital, LLC","portco_name":"eRESI","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"eRESI Secures Additional Investment from KKR","summary":"Mortgage funding platform eRESI secured a new investment from KKR-managed insurance accounts, which first invested in 2021.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2297ba28-bc30-47c2-80a1-507453e2bd18","evidence":"NEW YORK & CHARLOTTE, N.C.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--eRESI Capital, LLC (“eRESI” or the “Company”), an innovative mortgage funding platform that offers comprehensive private capital solutions to the residential mortgage market, today announced that it has secured a new investment from insurance accounts managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm. These insurance accounts initially invested in eRESI in 2021.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1d3b541addb2a6d262324871642865ee","date":"2024-10-24","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Enilive S.p.A","portco_name":"Enilive S.p.A Global","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Eni","round":null,"stake_pct":25.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Enilive to Accelerate Sustainable Mobility and the Energy Transition","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a 25% stake in Eni's mobility transformation company Enilive.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=e5ee83e3-1f32-4dae-9a85-329a1e0614c8","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of an agreement under which KKR will acquire a 25% stake in Enilive, Eni’s mobility transformation company dedicated to biorefining, biomethane production, smart mobility solutions, and providing services to support people on the move.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:2403fd20fe98f069b2f49c865391f3dc","date":"2025-02-18","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Enilive S.p.A","portco_name":"Enilive S.p.A Global","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Eni","round":null,"stake_pct":5.0,"amount":587500000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR To Make Further Investment In Enilive","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire an additional 5% of Enilive from Eni for €587.5 million, taking its holding to 30%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=57cf6773-eaf7-4800-8667-b4f88f9f874d","evidence":"London, 18th February 2025 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announces that KKR has signed an agreement to acquire an additional 5% stake in Enilive from Eni for a consideration of €587.5 million, taking its total holding in Enilive to 30%.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:bc8ce49c8186e7920ac52dbe51c6bc75","date":"2024-10-08","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"The Parking Spot","portco_name":"The Parking Spot","target_website":"theparkingspot.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Green Courte Partners, LLC","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Leading Near-Airport Parking Provider, The Parking Spot, from Green Courte Partners","summary":"KKR acquired near-airport parking operator The Parking Spot from an affiliate of Green Courte Partners; terms were not disclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ff460191-6e82-4f1c-adf9-1c02ab0d085b","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that KKR has acquired The Parking Spot (“TPS” or the “Company”), the nation’s leading owner and operator of near-airport parking properties, from an affiliate of Green Courte Partners, LLC, a private equity real estate investment firm. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ac596a61502b741f4ae3b79698cd242b","date":"2024-10-02","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Peregrine Energy Solutions LLC","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":250000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Peregrine Closes on Debt Financing from KKR","summary":"Energy storage developer Peregrine closed a credit facility from KKR insurance accounts able to finance up to $250 million in assets.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1fba8eea-a090-4c28-b6b3-dba918f38592","evidence":"BOULDER, Colo. and NEW YORK , Oct. 2, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Peregrine Energy Solutions LLC (\"Peregrine\"), an integrated multi-technology clean energy platform with a focus on utility-scale energy storage, and KKR, a leading global investment ﬁrm, today announced that Peregrine has closed on a credit facility from insurance accounts managed by KKR that can provide ﬁnancing for up to $250 million in assets.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:479c765a7141db58832780f4b585f651","date":"2024-09-25","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Queensland Airports Limited","portco_name":"Queensland Airports Limited","target_website":"qldairports.com.au","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Skip Essential Infrastructure Fund"],"seller":"The Infrastructure Fund (Macquarie Asset Management), State Super, Australian Retirement Trust","round":null,"stake_pct":74.25,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Consortium of KKR and the Skip Essential Infrastructure Fund to acquire Majority Stake in Queensland Airports","summary":"A KKR and Skip Essential Infrastructure Fund consortium agreed to acquire a 74.25% stake in Queensland Airports.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f9583a23-a2b5-4c31-be81-580fd1e8dd55","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and the Skip Essential Infrastructure Fund, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which a consortium of KKR (on behalf of funds managed by it) and the Skip Essential Infrastructure Fund (the ‘Consortium’) will acquire a 74.25% stake in Queensland Airports Limited (‘Queensland Airports’) from The Infrastructure Fund, managed by Macquarie Asset Management, State Super, and Australian Retirement Trust.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:6ecc8f6230d8683251950679f2911fe8","date":"2024-09-26","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"GeoStabilization International","portco_name":"GeoStabilization International","target_website":null,"investor":"Leonard Green & Partners, L.P.","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Sell GeoStabilization International to Leonard Green & Partners","summary":"KKR agreed to sell geohazard mitigation company GeoStabilization International to Leonard Green & Partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=272280f6-8dcd-46ad-abb1-5b3f22c1847b","evidence":"KKR today announced an agreement to sell GeoStabilization International (“GSI” or the “Company”) to Leonard Green & Partners, L.P. (“LGP”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:6acd94c3ff860da9cd502957be78502f","date":"2024-09-24","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"IQGeo","portco_name":"IQGeo","target_website":"iqgeo.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":333000000.0,"currency":"GBP","amount_basis":"equity_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Completes Acquisition of Geospatial Software Business IQGeo","summary":"KKR completed its £333 million acquisition of UK geospatial software developer IQGeo.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=26156e72-44a5-46a2-bc09-f45623cac762","evidence":"London, 24 September 2024 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the completion of its acquisition of IQGeo, a geospatial software developer headquartered in the U.K. KKR has acquired IQGeo for £333m and will be building on the company’s strong revenue growth.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:1dfeac48ca307b418516d9d56b9030ad","date":"2024-08-26","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Varsity Brands","portco_name":"Varsity Brands","target_website":"varsitybrands.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Bain Capital, Charlesbank","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Completes Acquisition of Varsity Brands from Bain Capital and Charlesbank","summary":"KKR completed its acquisition of Varsity Brands from Bain Capital and Charlesbank, becoming majority owner.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4cd89b41-e88a-423a-9703-b0502e71ebb0","evidence":"Varsity Brands (the “Company”), a leader in team sports, athletics and spirit, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the completion of the acquisition of Varsity Brands by KKR from Bain Capital and Charlesbank. As the new majority owner of Varsity Brands, KKR will support the Company as it continues to grow its business.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:88ad83eeffe6cf6ccb227a6c277ae2a2","date":"2024-08-08","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"FUJI SOFT INCORPORATED","portco_name":"FUJI SOFT","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Tender Offer to Acquire FUJI SOFT","summary":"KKR announced a tender offer at JPY 8,800 per share to acquire all shares of Japanese system integrator FUJI SOFT.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=90a762f7-0bf1-48bc-a608-b2d7a6bd5330","evidence":"TOKYO – August 8, 2024 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that FK Co., Ltd. (the “Offeror”), an entity owned by investment funds managed by KKR, intends to make a tender offer to acquire all the outstanding shares of FUJI SOFT INCORPORATED (“FUJI SOFT” or the “Company”; TSE stock code 9749). The proposed tender offer price of JPY 8,800 per share has been determined based on negotiations between KKR and FUJI SOFT.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:70aece5efd1cf62cf2ab821c14f4cf16","date":"2024-08-07","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"FGS Global","portco_name":"FGS Global","target_website":"fgsglobal.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"WPP","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1700000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to acquire majority position in FGS Global to support long-term growth; FGS to become standalone communications and public affairs consultancy","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire WPP's full equity position in FGS Global, building on its 2023 minority investment, in a deal valuing FGS at US$1.7 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8b3e2404-4349-4f33-90c8-a3e2b79554fd","evidence":"KKR today announced the acquisition of WPP’s full equity position in FGS Global (“FGS” or the “Company”), the preeminent global communications and public affairs consultancy. The proposed transaction is supported by FGS management, builds on KKR’s initial minority investment in July 2023, and values FGS at US $1.7 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0f4e7339728291dbc52aa15a04eeb4c2","date":"2024-07-30","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Avantus","portco_name":"Avantus","target_website":"avantus.com","investor":"KKR Capital Markets","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":522000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Avantus Announces Completion of Acquisition by KKR and Closing of $522 Million Development Facility","summary":"Avantus secured a $522 million development facility arranged by KKR Capital Markets and SMBC.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9103a8df-f10d-4a08-ae66-efdcae3e4de3","evidence":"Coinciding with the close of the transaction, Avantus has secured a $522 million development facility arranged by KKR Capital Markets and Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation (SMBC).","verified":true},{"key":"pr:12622c2d99f6b3e20d432ec8da6bf5af","date":"2024-07-25","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Instructure Holdings Inc.","portco_name":"Instructure Holdings Inc.","target_website":"instructure.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Dragoneer Investment Group"],"seller":"Thoma Bravo","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":4800000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Instructure to be Acquired by KKR for $4.8 Billion","summary":"Instructure agreed to be acquired by KKR funds, with Dragoneer participating, for $23.60 per share at an enterprise value of about $4.8 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=04bc08e0-3954-48cc-b85a-9ba5ae6e6c84","evidence":"SALT LAKE CITY, July 25, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Instructure Holdings, Inc. (NYSE: INST) (\"Instructure\"), a leading learning ecosystem, today announced that it has entered into a definitive agreement to be acquired by investment funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, for $23.60 per share in an all-cash transaction valued at an enterprise value of approximately $4.8 billion. KKR, with participation from Dragoneer Investment Group, will acquire all outstanding shares, including those shares owned by Instructure's existing majority owner, Thoma Bravo, a leading software investment firm, which took the company public in 2021.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:c4951fe25eb407ea254983b45e305b5c","date":"2024-07-24","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Metronet","portco_name":"MetroNet Fiber Inc","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["T-Mobile"],"seller":"Oak Hill Capital","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"T-Mobile and KKR Announce Joint Venture to Acquire Metronet and Offer Leading Fiber Solution to More U.S. Consumers","summary":"T-Mobile and KKR agreed to form a joint venture to acquire fiber provider Metronet, including Oak Hill Capital's stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=569516fb-febc-49dc-8921-28d7f650aa4c","evidence":"BELLEVUE, Wash. & NEW YORK & EVANSVILLE, Ind.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--T-Mobile (NASDAQ: TMUS), America's 5G leader and fastest-growing fixed wireless broadband provider, today announced it has entered into a definitive agreement to establish a joint venture (JV) with leading global investment firm KKR (NYSE: KKR) that will acquire Metronet including its broadband infrastructure, rapidly growing residential fiber business operations and existing customers. As part of the transaction, the JV will also acquire Oak Hill Capital’s existing stake.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:88a0513c8aa4e8a760c23708d29a4c3f","date":"2024-07-24","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Marmic Fire & Safety, Inc","portco_name":"Marmic Fire & Safety, Inc","target_website":"marmicfire.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"HGGC","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Marmic Fire & Safety","summary":"KKR funds acquired fire equipment inspection and maintenance provider Marmic Fire & Safety from HGGC.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=52d9ca49-a80b-4f0f-8f92-b82cb707f1ad","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that investment funds managed by KKR have acquired Marmic Fire & Safety (“Marmic” or the “Company”), a leading provider of regulation-mandated fire equipment inspection, testing and maintenance services, from HGGC.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:9ab077678a8f8611da7b3463ec176499","date":"2024-07-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Janney Montgomery Scott","portco_name":"Janney Montgomery Scott","target_website":"janney.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"The Penn Mutual Life Insurance Company","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Janney Montgomery Scott from Penn Mutual","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire wealth management and investment banking firm Janney Montgomery Scott from Penn Mutual.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=546270c5-1bc6-4c4f-8224-12e7cb0549c1","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm and The Penn Mutual Life Insurance Company (“Penn Mutual”) today announced the signing of a definitive agreement under which investment funds managed by KKR will acquire Janney Montgomery Scott LLC (“Janney” or the “Company”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4b6acb8ab808d538de8f63dd60ae3877","date":"2024-07-19","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Accountor Software","portco_name":"Accountor Software","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Vitruvian Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Accountor and Vitruvian announce KKR investment to support next chapter of growth","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in Finnish business software provider Accountor Software from Vitruvian Partners; terms were not disclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=356f58ed-1125-494e-ba03-8ae9acf46754","evidence":"Finland, 19 July 2024: Accountor Software, a leading provider of mission critical business software in Finland and Sweden, and selling majority shareholder Vitruvian Partners, today announced that KKR, a leading global investment firm, has agreed to acquire a majority stake in Accountor. Financial terms of the transaction, which is subject to customary closing conditions, were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:66790b29c599eab5659f893e2ea3b027","date":"2024-07-18","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Trinseo PLC","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":150000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Trinseo Announces New Receivables Financing Facility from KKR","summary":"Trinseo's receivables financing entity entered a $150 million non-recourse financing facility with KKR credit funds.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=6a831bde-e69b-4b3a-ac53-033e91981b27","evidence":"WAYNE, Pa. & NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Trinseo PLC (“Trinseo” or “the Company”)(NYSE: TSE), a specialty material solutions provider, today announced that a special purpose finance entity, Styron Receivables Funding Designated Activity Company, has entered into a $150 million non-recourse financing facility with credit funds and accounts managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:35076956c22797c08eafaba3bf705b97","date":"2024-07-09","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Nasuni","portco_name":"Nasuni","target_website":"nasuni.com","investor":"Vista Equity Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["TCV","KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":1200000000.0,"valuation_currency":"USD","headline":"Nasuni announces investment from Vista Equity Partners, KKR and TCV","summary":"Vista Equity Partners led a strategic growth investment in Nasuni joined by TCV and KKR, valuing the company at about $1.2 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d29eca63-ea01-4206-a30d-23a6d8a08dce","evidence":"BOSTON, July 9, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Nasuni, a leading enterprise data platform for modern hybrid cloud environments, today announced a strategic growth investment led by Vista Equity Partners, a global investment firm focused exclusively on enterprise software, data, and technology-enabled businesses. Vista will be joined by TCV and KKR in the new investment, which values Nasuni at approximately $1.2 billion.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:def503588b3833fb2b480178f3c9f1a5","date":"2024-06-30","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"SmartHR","portco_name":"SmartHR","target_website":"smarthr.jp","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Teachers' Venture Growth"],"seller":null,"round":"Series E","stake_pct":null,"amount":140000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Teachers’ Venture Growth Lead US$140 Million Series E Round in Leading Japanese Cloud-Native Human Resources Software Platform SmartHR","summary":"KKR and Teachers' Venture Growth jointly led a US$140 million Series E in Japanese HR software platform SmartHR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f87bb8bc-736a-4d70-85dc-7a033992311a","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Teachers’ Venture Growth (TVG), the late-stage venture and growth investment arm of Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which KKR (on behalf of funds managed by it) and TVG will jointly lead a US$140 million (JPY 21.4 billion) Series E fundraise of SmartHR (the ‘Company’), a leading cloud-native human resources management platform in Japan, with participation from existing shareholders.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:ec2245d219df4d8df65e9022e8809a10","date":"2024-07-01","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"BMH","portco_name":"BMH","target_website":"babymhospital.org","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Controlling Stake in Baby Memorial Hospital, a Multi-Specialty Hospital Network in India","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire a controlling stake in Indian multi-specialty hospital chain Baby Memorial Hospital.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3f620990-6f09-43c5-b467-2afe145c88e9","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Baby Memorial Hospital (‘BMH’), a leading regional multi-specialty hospital chain in India, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will acquire a controlling stake in BMH.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:dbb4b31e9f99b2a66e2a5da4b25bec2b","date":"2024-06-25","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"IGNIS P2X","portco_name":"Ignis","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["IGNIS"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":50.0,"amount":400000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and IGNIS announce partnership to develop green hydrogen, ammonia and other green technologies in Spain and internationally","summary":"KKR agreed to provide up to €400 million to launch IGNIS P2X, a 50/50 green hydrogen and ammonia platform with IGNIS.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=6ba7fd08-f147-466c-81d6-94c4825bd719","evidence":"Madrid, 25 June 2024 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, and IGNIS, a leading integrated global renewable group based in Spain, today announce an agreement to launch IGNIS P2X, a new Power-to-X (P2X) platform to develop primarily green hydrogen and ammonia projects for industrial applications in hard-to-abate sectors. As part of the joint venture agreement, KKR will provide up to €400 million to develop and build future projects. KKR and IGNIS will own 50% each of IGNIS P2X when launched, which will start with a global pipeline of P2X and renewable projects.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8cd9bdcbec8bb6ac6e692582bacf38e8","date":"2024-06-21","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Superstruct Entertainment","portco_name":"Superstruct Entertainment","target_website":"superstruct.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Providence Equity Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Pan-European Live Entertainment Group Superstruct from Providence Equity Partners","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire festival operator Superstruct Entertainment from Providence Equity Partners; terms were not disclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=e2649de6-c5ac-4093-a581-22f88fe76cf6","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announces the acquisition of Superstruct Entertainment (“Superstruct” or the “Company”), from Providence Equity Partners (“Providence”), a premier private equity firm specializing in growth-oriented investments in media, communications, education and technology. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:77a2af4f9d6246240a98eeee54ae95db","date":"2024-06-18","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"ST Telemedia Global Data Centres","portco_name":"ST Telemedia Global Data Centres","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Singtel"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1750000000.0,"currency":"SGD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"ST Telemedia Global Data Centres Raises S$1.75 Billion from KKR-Led Consortium with Singtel","summary":"A KKR-led consortium with Singtel agreed to invest S$1.75 billion in STT GDC via redeemable preference shares with warrants.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=108984f3-8a14-422d-8d9f-8edcbd8fc6b7","evidence":"ST Telemedia Global Data Centres (‘STT GDC’ or the ‘Company’), a leading data centre colocation services provider, KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Singtel, Asia’s leading communications technology group, today jointly announced the signing of definitive agreements under which a KKR-led consortium of KKR (on behalf of funds managed by it) and Singtel (the ‘Consortium’) will invest S$1.75 billion (~US$1.3 billion) in STT GDC. The transaction comprises an initial S$1.75 billion (~US$1.3 billion) investment by the Consortium via Redeemable Preference Shares (RPS), with detachable warrants.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:bb292dc9ae831305e4f65dcb4390b55f","date":"2024-06-11","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Quick Quack Car Wash","portco_name":"Quick Quack Car Wash","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Quick Quack Announces Strategic Investment by KKR","summary":"KKR funds made a significant minority investment in Quick Quack Car Wash alongside founders and Seidler Equity Partners.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=eb966bf9-7758-4c39-91c8-f6ca38cb7dc3","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm and Quick Quack Car Wash (“Quick Quack” or the “Company”) today announced that investment funds managed by KKR have made a significant minority investment in the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:42b645f8d2b07e15b58a2b8c2474588c","date":"2024-05-30","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Agiloft","portco_name":"Agiloft","target_website":"agiloft.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["FTV Capital","JMI Equity"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Majority Ownership in Agiloft","summary":"A KKR fund agreed to acquire a majority stake in contract lifecycle management software company Agiloft, with FTV Capital investing more and JMI Equity joining.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=6a24a111-16c3-4510-b364-86e1de9083ac","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that a fund managed by KKR has entered into an agreement to acquire a majority stake in Agiloft (“the Company”), a trusted global leader in data-first contract lifecycle management (“CLM”). As part of the transaction FTV Capital, a sector-focused growth equity firm and an existing investor in Agiloft, will make an additional investment in the Company, and JMI Equity, a growth equity firm focused on investing in leading software companies, will join as a new investor in the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ade828b202ae0c0e9f4b0c29c72d08a3","date":"2024-05-28","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Labrador Island Link","portco_name":"Labrador Island Link","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Emera Inc.","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1190000000.0,"currency":"CAD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Labrador Island Link Welcomes New Investor","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Emera's indirect minority equity interest in the Labrador Island Link transmission line in a C$1.19 billion transaction.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f4b9ab16-e670-4ec3-b45e-0739bb5f01e7","evidence":"JOHN’S, Newfoundland and Labrador--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Today, Emera Inc. (Emera), an international energy and services company, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced they have entered into a definitive agreement where KKR will acquire Emera’s indirect minority equity interest in the Labrador Island Link (LIL). The transaction value is $1.19 billion CAD, made up of $957 million CAD in cash and $235 million CAD for assuming Emera’s obligation to fund the remaining initial capital investment.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:6b06c20b4f9442fb7c1dca931c572d54","date":"2024-05-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Mirus Bio","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Merck","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":"Gamma Biosciences","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":600000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Gamma Biosciences Announces Sale of Mirus Bio to Merck for $600 Million","summary":"KKR-established Gamma Biosciences agreed to sell its operating company Mirus Bio to Merck for $600 million in cash.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=404a069f-df55-41b1-b1d9-b3c6543a7818","evidence":"MENLO PARK, Calif. and MADISON, Wis., May 23, 2024 - Gamma Biosciences, a life sciences platform established by KKR to address the advanced therapy bioprocessing market, today announced that it has entered into an agreement with Merck (XTRA:MRK), a leading science and technology company, whereby Merck will acquire Gamma operating company Mirus Bio for $600 million in cash.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:eba407c563095b485f8404d5bc3ab47e","date":"2024-05-21","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PHINMA Education","portco_name":"PHINMA Education","target_website":"phinma.edu.ph","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Kaizenvest"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Leading Filipino Higher Education Group PHINMA Education","summary":"KKR funds agreed to invest in Filipino higher education group PHINMA Education, its first Global Impact investment in the Philippines; PHINMA Corporation remains majority owner.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=bb43f357-027a-429e-8595-a129c322d23a","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and PHINMA Education Holdings, Inc. (‘PHINMA Education’ or the ‘Company’), a leading private higher education group and the education arm of Filipino conglomerate PHINMA Corporation, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will invest in PHINMA Education, with participation from existing shareholder Kaizenvest. PHINMA Corporation will remain the majority shareholder in PHINMA Education.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ea10c43a48c0f4ee42555764acdf94d5","date":"2024-05-21","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Infinx","portco_name":"Infinx","target_website":"infinx.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Norwest Venture Partners"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Healthcare Revenue Solutions Provider Infinx","summary":"A KKR fund acquired a significant minority stake in healthcare revenue cycle solutions provider Infinx.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=08959728-f5da-44a2-a39b-492393c9a8ea","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Infinx Services Private Limited (“Infinx” or the 'Company'), an AI-driven healthcare revenue cycle solutions provider, today announced the acquisition of a significant minority stake in Infinx by a KKR-managed fund. Norwest Venture Partners, an existing shareholder, also participated in the transaction.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:27fbba89b6113c2a7983c43cd00f2a04","date":"2024-05-06","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Healthium Medtech Ltd.","portco_name":"Healthium Medtech","target_website":"healthiummedtech.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Apax Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Healthium from Apax Funds","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire a controlling interest in Indian medical devices company Healthium from an Apax-advised fund.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=72df5ad6-3134-4b82-93cc-a72c7d230d8b","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which funds managed by KKR will acquire Healthium Medtech Ltd. (“Healthium”), a leading Indian medical devices company, from an affiliate of Funds advised by Apax Partners LLP (“Apax”), a leading global private equity advisory firm. The acquisition will be made by a special purpose vehicle owned by KKR-managed funds which will acquire a controlling interest in Healthium group, including Healthium.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:bbc20a1f0b051ae4ecb1d9a9bc860a1d","date":"2024-04-30","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Pacific Generation LLC","portco_name":"Pacific Generation LLC","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"PG&E Corporation","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"PG&E and KKR Enter Exclusive Talks on Strategic Partnership in Pacific Generation Transaction","summary":"PG&E entered exclusive negotiations to sell a minority interest in its Pacific Generation unit to KKR's infrastructure strategy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3691b982-a316-4648-a06a-70093f9cd1a9","evidence":"OAKLAND and MENLO PARK, Calif. – April 30, 2024 – PG&E Corporation (NYSE: PCG) (“PG&E”) today announced that it has entered into exclusive negotiations to sell a minority interest in Pacific Generation LLC (“Pacific Generation”) to KKR’s Infrastructure Strategy.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:bb5121c02f2de4d5e818a99459d8f522","date":"2024-04-25","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"nexeye","portco_name":"nexeye","target_website":"nexeye.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"3i Group plc","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"European Value-for-Money Optical Platform nexeye to be Acquired by KKR from 3i, Accelerating its Strategic Growth Ambitions","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire European value-for-money optical platform nexeye from 3i.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b323f737-c125-4d63-ac3f-ab0a12b51585","evidence":"Gorinchem (NL) / London (UK), 25 April 2024 – nexeye (the “Company” or “Group”) today announced that a definitive agreement has been signed whereby investment funds and accounts managed by KKR agreed to acquire the Company from investment firm 3i Group plc.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ab1a9ff302857d3174f535aebaf428bb","date":"2024-04-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Immedica Pharma","portco_name":"Immedica Pharma","target_website":"immedica.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Impilo"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Impilo Announce Strategic Partnership Together With Management in Rare Disease Platform Immedica Pharma","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire rare disease pharmaceutical company Immedica, with existing owner Impilo reinvesting to become an equal owner.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0eccf3aa-b128-4d90-abca-f48ab54a6acc","evidence":"Investment funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, have agreed to acquire Immedica Pharma, a pharmaceutical company headquartered in Stockholm, Sweden, focused on the commercialization of medicines for rare diseases and specialty care products. Existing owner, Nordic healthcare investment firm Impilo, will reinvest to become an equal owner alongside KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4e8e2a9d3fc01bb86d8ab99223534ccd","date":"2024-04-10","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Guesty","portco_name":"Guesty","target_website":"guesty.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Inovia Capital","Apax Funds","BDT & MSD Partners","Sixth Street"],"seller":null,"round":"Series F","stake_pct":null,"amount":130000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Guesty Raises $130M to Accelerate Global Expansion","summary":"Short-term rental software company Guesty raised a $130 million Series F led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5963566f-1716-4dbd-a895-f28068639b78","evidence":"NEW YORK, April 10, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Guesty, the leading property management software platform for the short-term rental (\"STR\") and hospitality industry, today announced a $130M Series F funding round led by leading global investment firm KKR. Inovia Capital, together with existing investors Apax Funds, BDT & MSD Partners and Sixth Street, also joined the round, extending their support following Guesty's significant expansion and sustained growth.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0e4062726b39fbf71f9593bc757b9394","date":"2024-04-02","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Sunfire","portco_name":"Sunfire","target_website":"sunfireinc.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Stone Point Capital","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"SunFire Announces Investment from KKR","summary":"Insurance distribution software platform SunFire was acquired by KKR funds, with previous majority owner Stone Point remaining a significant minority shareholder.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=81bf2478-bbec-4810-99c8-1f2c84a7d06a","evidence":"SunFireMatrix, Inc. (“SunFire” or the “Company”), a leading software and tech-enabled services platform serving the insurance distribution and health plan markets, announced today that it has been acquired by funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm. Funds managed by Stone Point Capital LLC, the Company’s previous majority owner, will continue to be a significant minority shareholder in the Company. Financial details of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5fa3b32290e0ac534186568ff4e69c9f","date":"2024-03-25","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"KBS","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Ares Management","BlackRock"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KBS Announces Recapitalization","summary":"Facility services provider KBS was recapitalized by long-time investors KKR, Ares and BlackRock, which become majority equity holders.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=530067e8-9faa-456e-b9fa-f318dad0e01e","evidence":"OCEANSIDE, Calif., March 25, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- KBS, a leading privately held facility services provider in North America, announced today a recapitalization by investment funds and accounts managed by its long-time investors KKR (\"KKR\"), Ares Management (\"Ares\") and Blackrock Capital Investment Advisors, LLC or affiliates thereof (\"BlackRock\"), which will become majority equity holders in the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:9328cb5ee2ae0cdb519ba69bce32f05f","date":"2024-03-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Avantus","portco_name":"Avantus","target_website":"avantus.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["EIG"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Avantus to Support Renewable Energy Deployment in the United States","summary":"KKR funds agreed to acquire a majority stake in US solar and storage developer Avantus, with EIG remaining the other equity investor.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=df1696e8-3969-49d2-8a82-9ba4533a9a52","evidence":"Today, KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced the signing of a definitive agreement pursuant to which investment funds and accounts managed by KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in Avantus, a premier U.S. developer of large utility-scale solar and solar-plus-storage projects. Following the close of the transaction, KKR and existing investor EIG, a leading institutional investor in the global energy and infrastructure sectors, will be the sole equity investors in Avantus.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7683213850e8f501fdcc1e89ddd7b3b6","date":"2024-03-15","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ottobock","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1100000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to support Ottobock with capital solution","summary":"A KKR co-led investor consortium agreed to provide a €1.1 billion financing solution to Ottobock, supporting the Näder family's buyback of EQT's stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f1c002e8-a7e1-411b-b892-44c7620012f6","evidence":"London and Frankfurt, 15 March, 2024 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, announces today that a consortium of investors, co-led by KKR, has agreed to provide a €1.1 billion financing solution to support the future growth of Ottobock (the “Company”), a global market leader in prosthetics. The financing will also support existing majority shareholder Professor Hans Georg Näder and the Näder Family’s buy back of EQT’s shareholding in the business.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:60c5ce973133ec8625d1dbcf3e6e2561","date":"2024-03-14","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Encavis AG","portco_name":"Encavis AG","target_website":"encavis.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Viessmann"],"seller":"ABACON CAPITAL","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to invest in Encavis AG to accelerate the Company’s long-term growth","summary":"A KKR-led consortium including Viessmann signed an investment agreement with Encavis and launched a takeover offer at EUR 17.50 per share.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c1b41f4d-24a2-44ba-887f-b31007f12e20","evidence":"March 14, 2024 – Today, Blitz 21-823 AG (in future: Elbe BidCo AG, “BidCo”), a holding company controlled by investment funds, vehicles and accounts advised and managed by Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. As part of the transaction, BidCo will launch a voluntary public takeover offer for all outstanding free float shares of the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:0875460f6d2b1d3d4b38444aa1697214","date":"2024-03-13","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"HarbourView Equity Partners","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Kuvare Asset Management"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"HarbourView Equity Partners Secures Close to $500 Million in Debt Financing from KKR and Other Investors to Expand Music Investment Opportunities","summary":"HarbourView secured about $500 million in debt financing via a music royalty securitization led by KKR insurance vehicles.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0a930e25-cfc5-40eb-a3ac-ea145ad32e7f","evidence":"NEWARK, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--HarbourView Equity Partners (HarbourView), an industry-leading alternative asset management company focused on investment opportunities in the sports, media and entertainment space, has secured approximately $500 million in debt financing through a private securitization backed by its diversified catalog of music royalties. Insurance vehicles and accounts managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm, led the financing and investment accounts advised by Kuvare Asset Management also participated in the transaction.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:ec1037c238bd9f7e658251882dcd6324","date":"2024-03-11","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"mdf commerce inc.","portco_name":"mdf commerce inc.","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":255000000.0,"currency":"CAD","amount_basis":"equity_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Mdf Commerce Enters Definitive Agreement To Be Acquired By KKR","summary":"mdf commerce agreed to be acquired by KKR for C$5.80 per share, or C$255 million in total equity value.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1b943ed2-ee58-4132-9b24-2674d9009429","evidence":"mdf commerce shareholders to receive C$5.80 in cash per share, representing C$255 million in total equity value and a premium of approximately 58% to the closing price of the common shares on the TSX on March 8, 2024","verified":true},{"key":"pr:49a03d5ef2160a875b4f856f31966f56","date":"2024-02-26","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Omnissa","portco_name":"Omnissa","target_website":"omnissa.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Broadcom Inc.","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":4000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Broadcom’s End-User Computing Division","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Broadcom's End-User Computing Division (later Omnissa) in a transaction valued at about $4 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=48701629-ae4d-4d88-b1a9-90a438c6bf6c","evidence":"KKR today announced the signing of a definitive agreement with Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ: AVGO) to acquire its End-User Computing Division (the “EUC Division”) in a transaction valued at approximately $4 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:3a16c4fe1770a28594485c2379338168","date":"2024-02-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Chord Music Partners","portco_name":"Chord Music Partners","target_website":null,"investor":"Dundee Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":["Universal Music Group"],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1850000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to sell majority stake in Chord Music Partners to Universal Music Group and Dundee Partners led Investor Consortium","summary":"KKR agreed to sell its majority stake in Chord Music Partners to a Dundee Partners-led consortium, with UMG buying 25.8% for US$240 million in a deal valuing Chord at US$1.85 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=77ff422d-1909-4521-b4e5-4e4bf6178e3a","evidence":"KKR to sell its majority stake in Chord to current shareholder Dundee Partners and its investor consortium with a minority stake held by UMG SANTA MONICA, Calif. and HILVERSUM, The Netherlands, Feb. 20, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Universal Music Group (UMG), the world-leader in music-based entertainment, and Dundee Partners, the investment office of the Hendel family, today announced that UMG will acquire a 25.8% interest in Chord Music Partners (Chord) for US$240 million (approximately €223 million when translated into € at today's current EUR/USD rate), in a deal that values Chord at US$1.85 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:50b3f9796ec5d6c0e7635a60cea9ff7e","date":"2024-02-16","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Clarience Technologies","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Leads Financing for Clarience Technologies’ Acquisition of Safe Fleet","summary":"KKR served as lead arranger, administrative agent and investor on debt financing for Clarience Technologies' acquisition of Safe Fleet.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=11c234e3-a273-4418-ab46-08cd5a27bc84","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that it served as Lead Arranger, Administrative Agent, and investor on a debt financing for Clarience Technologies’ Acquisition of Safe Fleet. KKR invested in the transaction through its credit vehicles and accounts.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:22caf945f8258d6e1049881f3100a40f","date":"2024-02-15","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"MB2 Dental","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2344000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"MB2 Dental Raises US$2.344bn Unitranche Debt Facility With KKR","summary":"Dental partnership organization MB2 Dental closed a US$2.344 billion unitranche debt facility led and arranged by KKR credit vehicles.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=cc90b283-6a20-42a8-a55e-6c229e781b63","evidence":"DALLAS--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Leading dental partnership organization (“DPO”), MB2 Dental has closed a US$2.344bn unitranche debt facility with credit vehicles and accounts managed by KKR, which acted as Lead Investor and Arranger on the transaction.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:59647b0676a797b2794c05ff29a5d9e4","date":"2024-02-14","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Cotiviti","portco_name":"Cotiviti","target_website":"cotiviti.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Veritas Capital"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cotiviti Announces Recapitalization with KKR and Long-Standing Owner Veritas","summary":"Cotiviti agreed a recapitalization under which KKR and long-standing owner Veritas become co-sponsors with equal ownership stakes.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ced6af48-9213-49ab-85fa-83523f6865ce","evidence":"SALT LAKE CITY, February 14, 2024 – Cotiviti (“the Company”), a leading healthcare data and technology business, announced today that the Company has entered into a definitive agreement to recapitalize the business with affiliates of its long-standing partner Veritas Capital (“Veritas”), a leading investor at the intersection of technology and government, and investment funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm. Under the agreement, KKR and Veritas will become co-sponsors with equal ownership stakes in Cotiviti.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7c0f6cac687972b6e7711d8ff81f3062","date":"2024-01-23","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Optio Investment Partners","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Kennedy Lewis Investment Management","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":750000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Optio Investment Partners, Kennedy Lewis Investment Management and KKR announce multi-year financing agreement","summary":"Kennedy Lewis and KKR agreed to provide asset-based funding of up to USD 750 million initially for Optio's Auto Evolution leasing and subscription strategy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=101a3bae-a600-42c0-832f-cf8c3669c444","evidence":"Under this agreement, Kennedy Lewis and KKR will provide asset-based funding to support the Optio Auto Evolution strategy, driving next generation auto financing. The agreement commenced in December 2023 with an initial commitment of up to USD 750 million to fund the Optio Auto Evolution leasing and subscription strategy for retail and business customers across the UK.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8fb97f812e2adbead7a8f9a25ca13f43","date":"2023-12-07","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Cortex","portco_name":"Cortex","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Hellman & Friedman","AI Life Sciences"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":90000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ajax Health Establishes Cortex, a Comprehensive AFib Ablation Technology Company, with $90 Million Investment Led by KKR and Hellman & Friedman","summary":"Ajax Health established AFib ablation company Cortex with $90 million of funding commitments led by KKR and Hellman & Friedman.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f212daea-7f0f-4e96-9def-09cbaf21228c","evidence":"Cortex has raised $90 million in funding commitments led by KKR and Hellman & Friedman (H&F) with participation by other investors including AI Life Sciences, an affiliate of Access Industries.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:5f8ff42fc5b87d7bcea0175b608139ae","date":"2023-11-30","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Maverix Medical","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Hologic, Inc.","Ajax Health"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR, Hologic and Ajax Health Create New Platform to Accelerate Medical Device Innovation","summary":"KKR and Hologic invested to establish lung cancer detection device platform Maverix Medical, managed by Ajax Health.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d192153c-b202-4b71-9267-d8d5699f3210","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced a new platform established with investments from KKR and Hologic, Inc. (Nasdaq: HOLX), a global leader in women’s health and medical technology innovator. The new platform, named Maverix Medical, will be managed by Ajax Health under the leadership of Duke Rohlen.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:c67e0bc2712c6b78b1125f22d8edefa4","date":"2023-11-29","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Global Atlantic Financial Group","portco_name":"Global Atlantic Financial Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":37.0,"amount":2700000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Remaining 37% of Global Atlantic for $2.7 Billion in All-Cash Transaction","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire the remaining 37% of insurer Global Atlantic for an estimated $2.7 billion in cash, taking ownership to 100%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=32c8aac4-81bd-4bd0-a0ab-2c9ec9867ec3","evidence":"KKR & Co. Inc. (NYSE: KKR) and Global Atlantic Financial Group LLC (“Global Atlantic” or “GA”) today announced a definitive agreement under which KKR will acquire the remaining 37% stake of leading insurance company Global Atlantic, increasing KKR’s ownership to 100%. The total cash purchase price is currently estimated to be approximately $2.7 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:45cac34a253d13d4b69003bcff8b90a4","date":"2023-11-27","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Potter Global Technologies","portco_name":"Potter Global Technologies","target_website":"potterglobaltech.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Gryphon Investors","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Potter Global Technologies","summary":"KKR funds acquired fire and life safety equipment maker Potter Global Technologies from Gryphon Investors.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5d6c9647-4ba4-4463-91ad-a0c79ad73ab7","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that investment funds managed by KKR have acquired Potter Global Technologies (“Potter” or the “Company”), a leading manufacturer of fire and life safety equipment, from Gryphon Investors.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f901ca8f928e066a9c5b83eb2335bc83","date":"2023-11-15","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"United Malt Group Limited","portco_name":"United Group (SBB/Telemach)","target_website":null,"investor":"Malteries Soufflet","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1500000000.0,"currency":"AUD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR supports InVivo in the global expansion of Malteries Soufflet","summary":"KKR supported Malteries Soufflet in funding its AUD 1.5 billion acquisition of United Malt Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=40885dd7-6147-440e-b5c5-89a085554927","evidence":"Paris, 15 November, 2023 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, announces today that it has supported Malteries Soufflet in the funding and execution of the AUD 1.5 billion acquisition of United Malt Group Limited (“United Malt”), the fourth largest maltster globally.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:182a38f3f76dfb218a396a66de240ddc","date":"2023-11-15","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Malteries Soufflet","portco_name":"Malteries Soufflet","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Bpifrance","Crédit Agricole Group"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":550000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR supports InVivo in the global expansion of Malteries Soufflet","summary":"KKR led a combined €550 million follow-on investment in Malteries Soufflet with Bpifrance and Crédit Agricole to fund the United Malt acquisition.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=40885dd7-6147-440e-b5c5-89a085554927","evidence":"To fund the United Malt acquisition, KKR, with participation from Bpifrance and Crédit Agricole Group, led a combined follow-on investment of €550m.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:fd997ae24c0062ea4275a9f8d5a2ed3c","date":"2023-10-29","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"OMS Group","portco_name":"OMS Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":400000000.0,"currency":