leading global investment firm, today announced the combination of Cardenas Markets and Mi Pueblo, two Hispanic grocery chains in which KKR made significant investments last year, alongside Victory Park Capital.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:61abfce8de93445577c4b94555588a68","date":"2017-06-30","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Australian Venue Co","portco_name":"Australian Venue Co","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Partner with Dixon Hospitality","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in Australian hospitality group Dixon Hospitality (later Australian Venue Co).","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d9a88eea-7ac8-4206-9fc6-460e17722b61","evidence":"MELBOURNE, Australia & SYDNEY--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading Australian hospitality and leisure group Dixon Hospitality Limited (“Dixon Hospitality” or the “Company”) and global investment firm KKR today announced a partnership under which KKR will acquire a majority stake in the Company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:8d2f38add2b46fa384ceac6302f34c29","date":"2017-06-14","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Q-Park N.V.","portco_name":"Q-Park N.V.","target_website":"q-park.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"100% Of Q-Park Shareholders Accept Offer of KKR Infrastructure","summary":"KKR announced that 100% of Q-Park shareholders accepted its infrastructure offer for all shares of the European car park operator.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=eafcb342-0ce8-4cef-b4ef-09195ff3edb8","evidence":"LONDON & MAASTRICHT, the Netherlands--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, has today announced that 100% of the shareholders of Q-Park N.V. (Q-Park) have accepted its offer for all shares in Q-Park.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:0955c6a3fdf75a80fa908094dc0787e3","date":"2017-06-01","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PAAMCO Prisma Holdings","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":39.9,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and PAAMCO Announce Completion of Strategic Transaction to Create PAAMCO Prisma Holdings","summary":"KKR and PAAMCO completed the combination of PAAMCO and KKR's Prisma Capital Partners into PAAMCO Prisma, with KKR owning 39.9%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2b306b98-9fa6-4e25-b467-2b948999e89d","evidence":"KKR and PAAMCO Announce Completion of Strategic Transaction to Create PAAMCO Prisma Holdings RVINE, Calif. and NEW YORK, June 1, 2017 /PRNewswire/ -- KKR and Pacific Alternative Asset Management Company, LLC (\"PAAMCO\") today announced the completion of their strategic transaction to combine PAAMCO and Prisma Capital Partners LP (\"Prisma\") to create PAAMCO Prisma Holdings, LLC (\"PAAMCO Prisma\"). The business is majority employee-owned, with employees of PAAMCO Prisma Holdings owning 60.1% of the business and KKR owning a 39.9% interest as a long-term strategic partner.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:03261b55d2241e841aaca0856d98395c","date":"2017-05-08","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Pandora","portco_name":"Pandora","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":150000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Pandora Announces $150 Million Investment by KKR","summary":"Pandora agreed a $150 million strategic investment from KKR in Series A convertible preferred stock.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=158ee1d9-d611-4250-8e89-e1f0cdaa868f","evidence":"OAKLAND, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Pandora (NYSE: P) today announced it has entered into an agreement for a $150 million strategic investment from KKR. Under the terms of the investment, KKR will purchase an aggregate of $150 million in a new designated Series A convertible preferred stock of Pandora.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:99cf76233fdbda101cdc6e9e7ae78e0a","date":"2017-05-04","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Sentio Healthcare Properties","portco_name":"Sentio Healthcare Properties","target_website":null,"investor":"Kayne Anderson Real Estate Advisors","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":825000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Kayne Anderson Real Estate Advisors to Acquire KKR-Backed Sentio Healthcare Properties in an $825 Million Transaction","summary":"Kayne Anderson Real Estate Advisors agreed to acquire KKR-backed Sentio Healthcare Properties in an all-cash merger based on an estimated total asset value of $825 million.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2e395788-fe5f-4ca9-8b66-4bfb7ae35969","evidence":"BOCA RATON, Fla. and ORLANDO, Fla., May 4, 2017 /PRNewswire/ -- Kayne Anderson Real Estate Advisors (\"KAREA\"), the real estate private equity arm of Kayne Anderson Capital Advisors, L.P., Sentio Healthcare Properties, Inc. (\"Sentio\" or the \"REIT\"), Sentio Investments, LLC (the \"Advisor\" or \"Sentio Investments\") and KKR (NYSE: KKR) today announced a definitive merger agreement under which affiliates of KAREA will acquire Sentio by way of merger. Under the terms of the agreement, which was unanimously approved by the board of directors of Sentio, KAREA will acquire all of the outstanding shares of Sentio in an all-cash transaction based on an estimated total asset value of $825 million.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a21ae69fba79b38c6b43240709627907","date":"2017-05-02","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Advanced Cardiac Therapeutics","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Ajax Health","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":["New Enterprise Associates","Questa Capital Management"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":45000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Advanced Cardiac Therapeutics Announces $45 Million in New Funding to Advance Innovative Treatment for Heart Disease","summary":"Advanced Cardiac Therapeutics raised $45 million in new equity funding led by KKR-backed Ajax Health.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1fd1dcce-f26a-448b-9380-0c2e3c95cfff","evidence":"SANTA CLARA, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Advanced Cardiac Therapeutics, Inc., (“ACT” or the “Company”), a medical device company focused on developing a next-generation ablation catheter to treat cardiac arrhythmias including atrial fibrillation, today announced $45 million in new equity funding led by Ajax Health (“Ajax”) alongside existing investor New Enterprise Associates (“NEA”) and new investor Questa Capital Management (“Questa”).","verified":true},{"key":"pr:d0fde3b3af8f83aca7fa3f4fd9a563dd","date":"2017-04-26","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ivalua","portco_name":"Ivalua","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":"growth","stake_pct":null,"amount":70000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ivalua Raises $70M from KKR","summary":"Spend management software company Ivalua raised $70 million in growth equity minority funding from KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5c4f22bd-d71f-4e65-aafe-136d27515120","evidence":"SAN FRANCISCO, NEW YORK, PARIS & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Ivalua, a market-leading Spend Management software company, headquartered in Redwood City, California and Paris, today announced that it has raised a $70M growth equity minority funding from KKR, a leading global investor, to realize its ambition of becoming the global leader in the fast-growing Spend Management Market. KKR will become a new shareholder alongside the Founders and Ardian, which invested in Ivalua in 2011.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8a5aee46e35c59d3d875c15a20fd6c0b","date":"2017-04-26","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Hitachi Kokusai Electric","portco_name":"Hitachi Kokusai Electric","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Japan Industrial Partners","Hitachi"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":257100000000.0,"currency":"JPY","amount_basis":"equity_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Tender Offer to Acquire Hitachi Kokusai Electric","summary":"A KKR-owned entity announced a tender offer for Hitachi Kokusai Electric at a price valuing the company at about JPY 257.1 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=248f7f4b-749a-41aa-9101-e56a52bf1bdd","evidence":"TOKYO--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR, Hitachi Ltd., (“Hitachi”) and Japan Industrial Partners, Inc. (“JIP”) today announced that HKE Holdings G.K. (the “Offeror”), an entity owned by investment funds managed by KKR, intends to make a tender offer for the common shares of Hitachi Kokusai Electric Inc. (“Hitachi Kokusai” or the “Company”; TSE stock code 6756). Since the total number of Hitachi Kokusai’s outstanding shares (excluding treasury shares) is equal to 102,703,392 (as of March 31, 2017), the proposed tender offer price values Hitachi Kokusai at approximately JPY 257.1 billion (approx. US$2.3 billion at the exchange rate of US$1=JPY111).","verified":true},{"key":"pr:5b76164789cb6f4eaa347bad9ba2b985","date":"2017-04-18","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Focus Financial Partners","portco_name":"Focus Financial Partners","target_website":null,"investor":"Stone Point Capital","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":"Centerbridge Partners, Summit Partners, Polaris Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Focus Financial Partners To Receive Significant Investment from Stone Point Capital and KKR","summary":"An investor group led by Stone Point and KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in Focus Financial Partners at a valuation of about $2 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=717acf51-c49b-459a-85d8-4604f63c647c","evidence":"NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Focus Financial Partners (‘Focus'), a leading international partnership of independent, fiduciary wealth management firms, announced today that an investor group led by Stone Point Capital (‘Stone Point') and KKR will acquire a majority stake in the company, which values Focus at approximately $2 billion. Selling shareholders include Focus' existing private equity investors, Centerbridge Partners, Summit Partners and Polaris Partners, as well as certain wealth management affiliates and employees.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8e4c00755c8b36fe016695992ee76e42","date":"2017-04-11","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Lyft","portco_name":"Lyft","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":"Series G","stake_pct":null,"amount":600000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Lyft","summary":"KKR closed a primary investment in Lyft as part of its $600 million Series G round.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=194535e4-a765-4e89-ac07-f657021cf2ee","evidence":"NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the closing of a primary investment in Lyft, a leading ridesharing platform in the U.S. The investment is part of a $600 million Series G round of funding into the company.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:2ea206c72378bf21ec26f8e72947ffa5","date":"2017-04-03","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Angelica Corporation","portco_name":"Angelica Corporation","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":125000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Angelica Corporation Enters into Asset Purchase Agreement with KKR","summary":"A KKR affiliate agreed to acquire substantially all of healthcare linen provider Angelica's assets in a transaction valued at about $125 million plus assumed liabilities.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=17eec868-2595-4b02-80a4-feecaeb9bf34","evidence":"ALPHARETTA, Ga., April 3, 2017 /PRNewswire/ -- Angelica Corporation (\"Angelica\" or the \"Company\"), the leader in healthcare linen and medical laundry services, today announced that it has entered into an asset purchase agreement (\"APA\") with an entity affiliated with KKR, under which the KKR affiliate will acquire substantially all of Angelica's assets as a going concern in a transaction valued at approximately $125 million plus certain assumed liabilities.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:113a10afaacd0ef3216f95b62c7c8015","date":"2017-03-28","date_text":null,"kind":"secondary","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Bharti Infratel","portco_name":"Bharti Infratel","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Canada Pension Plan Investment Board"],"seller":"Bharti Airtel Limited","round":null,"stake_pct":10.3,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Bharti Airtel completes secondary sale of 10.3% stake in Bharti Infratel to a consortium of KKR & Canada Pension Plan Investment Board (CPPIB)","summary":"Bharti Airtel completed the sale of a 10.3% stake in Bharti Infratel to a KKR and CPPIB consortium for over INR 6,193.9 crore.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f7079c8b-80e2-474c-b27a-bb30b8c54ff1","evidence":"New Delhi, March 28, 2017: Bharti Airtel Limited (“Bharti Airtel”), India’s largest telecommunications services provider, today announced the successful completion of the secondary sale of over 190 million shares of its subsidiary Bharti Infratel Limited (“Bharti Infratel”) representing 10.3%, to a consortium of funds advised by KKR and Canada Pension Plan Investment Board (“CPPIB”) for a total consideration of over INR 6,193.9 Cr (approx. US$ 951.6 million), executed at a price of Rs. 325 per share.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:51a5f52bf85beaa41284e69a70e29607","date":"2017-03-17","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"USI Insurance Services LLC","portco_name":"USI Insurance Services LLC","target_website":"usi.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["CDPQ"],"seller":"Onex Corporation","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":4300000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and CDPQ Acquire USI, a Leading Insurance Brokerage and Consulting Firm","summary":"KKR and CDPQ agreed to jointly acquire USI from Onex in a transaction valuing it at US$4.3 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3be36fca-22fe-4209-ab81-9c23249bde5e","evidence":"NEW YORK & MONTRÉAL--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR and CDPQ, along with USI employees, announced today their joint acquisition of USI Insurance Services (USI), a leading U.S. insurance brokerage and consulting firm. As partners with equal ownership, KKR and CDPQ will acquire USI from Onex Corporation and its affiliates in a transaction that values USI at US$4.3 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:33a84332a178518254693674564c37b3","date":"2017-02-27","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Cherwell Software","portco_name":"Cherwell Software","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":50000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cherwell Software Secures $50 Million Investment from KKR to Further Advance Service Management Leadership","summary":"Cherwell Software secured $50 million in funding from KKR's Next Generation Technology Fund.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3988f676-57c0-4b01-b6f4-1f69b00b6a6b","evidence":"COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo., Feb. 27, 2017 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Cherwell Software, LLC, a leading provider of IT service management (ITSM) solutions, announced today that it has secured $50 million in funding from KKR, a global investment firm. KKR is making the investment through its Next Generation Technology Fund, which focuses on investments in software, security, Internet, digital media, and information services.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:214eae6c73691a8f1aaf42b30fd43f2c","date":"2017-02-26","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Gambol Pet Group","portco_name":"Gambol Pet Group","target_website":"gambolpet.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in China’s Gambol Pet Group","summary":"KKR invested in Chinese pet food maker Gambol Pet Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=35f9995b-baff-48de-90a6-6dff60cf33b7","evidence":"BEIJING & LIAOCHENG, CHINA--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Global investment firm KKR has invested in Gambol Pet Group (the “Company” or “Gambol”), a leading provider of high-quality pet food headquartered in Shandong Province, China.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:00e9b2b30bcf4ade3a8d6ad915efe60d","date":"2017-02-21","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Telxius","portco_name":"Telxius","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Telefonica","round":null,"stake_pct":40.0,"amount":3678000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Partners with Telefonica to Further Develop Telxius","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire up to 40% of Telefonica's telecom infrastructure company Telxius at an implied enterprise value of €3.678bn.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=71f72dcf-cbfc-48ae-9dcc-553394f219f5","evidence":"KKR Partners with Telefonica to Further Develop TelxiusLONDON & MADRID--(BUSINESS WIRE)--KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announces that it has agreed to acquire a stake of up to 40 per cent in Telxius, a leading critical telecom infrastructure owner & service provider in Europe and Americas. The deal implies an enterprise value of €3.678bn and is subject to the customary closing conditions.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:50c4f208d19c67c8c8ea31c695e44f99","date":"2017-02-13","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Travelopia","portco_name":"Travelopia","target_website":"travelopia.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"TUI AG","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Travelopia from TUI","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire specialist travel group Travelopia from TUI.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f2d59497-0591-44f3-956e-6d62179cd3d2","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announces that it has agreed to acquire Travelopia (the “Company”) from TUI AG (“TUI”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ea108850fc187ecdd42d7322f5f71b9b","date":"2017-02-06","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PAAMCO Prisma Holdings","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":39.9,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"PAAMCO and KKR Prisma Form Strategic Partnership to Create New Liquid Alternatives Investment Firm","summary":"KKR agreed to combine KKR Prisma with PAAMCO into PAAMCO Prisma Holdings, retaining a 39.9% stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0baeb672-d6eb-4575-97db-5435f3114208","evidence":"KKR Prisma and PAAMCO will combine to form a new firm, PAAMCO Prisma Holdings, which will have over $30 billion in assets The combined business will be majority employee-owned with employees of PAAMCO and KKR Prisma owning 60.1% of the combined business and KKR retaining a 39.9% ownership stake as a long-term strategic partner","verified":null},{"key":"pr:58d5cd81c386f021fd02adbfb94dceb8","date":"2017-01-13","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Koki Holdings Co., Ltd","portco_name":"Koki Holdings Co., Ltd","target_website":"koki-holdings.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Hitachi Ltd.","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Tender Offer to Acquire Hitachi Koki Hitachi and Hitachi Urban Investment Agree to Tender Their Holdings of Hitachi Koki Shares","summary":"A KKR-owned entity announced a tender offer for Hitachi Koki (later Koki Holdings) at JPY 870 per share after a JPY 580 special dividend, valuing shares at JPY 1,450.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=15942a31-4650-4ef2-845d-90b95e2c0415","evidence":"TOKYO--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR today announced that HK Holdings Co., Ltd. (the “Bidder”), an entity owned by investment funds controlled by KKR, intends to make a tender offer for all the existing common shares and stock acquisition rights of leading power tool and life science equipment manufacturer Hitachi Koki Co., Ltd. (“Hitachi Koki” or the “Company”) (Code number: 6581, First Section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange). The Bidder has set a value of Hitachi Koki common shares of JPY 1,450 per common share. Assuming the payment of the Special Dividend of JPY 580 per common share upon the success of the Tender Offer, the Bidder has set a tender offer price per common share of JPY 870.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b7c4609899adda1721023acccb409e4c","date":"2017-01-05","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Slayback Pharma","portco_name":"Slayback Pharma","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":60000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Slayback Pharma Announces $60 Million in New Financing by KKR","summary":"Slayback Pharma closed a $60 million financing commitment from KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c9ec03f8-e3b0-454c-bdd1-cd44394047e4","evidence":"PRINCETON JUNCTION, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Slayback Pharma, LLC (“Slayback”), a privately held pharmaceutical research and development company, announced today the closing of a $60 million commitment by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a56c1be33806d4842af969faeb6cc3b3","date":"2017-01-05","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Cerêve","portco_name":"Cerêve","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Versant Ventures","Arboretum Ventures","Partner Ventures"],"seller":null,"round":"Series B","stake_pct":null,"amount":38000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cerêve Raises $38 Million to Fuel Launch of Insomnia Device in New Financing Led by KKR","summary":"Insomnia device maker Cerêve closed a $38 million Series B led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=28d2c833-ab9c-4a2b-aa26-df30791003d7","evidence":"OAKMONT, Pa.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Cerêve Inc., a privately-held health care company preparing to launch its FDA-cleared insomnia device, announced today the closing of a $38 million Series B round of financing led by KKR, a leading global investment firm. Also participating in the financing are existing shareholders Versant Ventures, Arboretum Ventures, and Partner Ventures.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:42e145d4c42c6dbf57dd68405ab36fbd","date":"2016-12-15","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Capsugel","portco_name":"Capsugel","target_website":null,"investor":"Lonza Group AG","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":5500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Lonza to Acquire Capsugel to Create Leading Integrated Solutions Provider to the Global Pharma and Consumer Healthcare Industries","summary":"Lonza agreed to acquire Capsugel from KKR for USD 5.5 billion in cash, including refinancing about USD 2 billion of debt.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=fae2b950-3721-403f-a04d-2bafc48ee01b","evidence":"Lonza Group AG (\"Lonza,\" VTX: LONN.VX), KKR and Capsugel S.A. (\"Capsugel\") today announced that they have entered into a definitive agreement under which Lonza will acquire Capsugel from KKR for USD 5.5 billion in cash, including refinancing of existing Capsugel debt of approximately USD 2 billion, through a transaction that has been approved by the Boards of Directors of both Lonza and Capsugel.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0dd2e416ca45d2c7bbe209f2330e5457","date":"2016-12-15","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Dentix","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":200000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"With the Financial Advice of BBVA: Dentix Reaches Agreement with KKR to Boost Its International Expansion with €200m of Credit Financing","summary":"KKR agreed to provide €200m of long-term credit financing to Spanish dental chain Dentix.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=bb466b50-d6db-447e-ab75-646a4b41460b","evidence":"MADRID--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Dentix, a leading company in the dental industry in Spain, has signed a strategic financing agreement with KKR, a leading global investment firm, who will provide €200m of long-term credit financing to the Company to boost its international expansion plan.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:be44d20a55c8d1d563c7ecdaff8cb439","date":"2016-12-15","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Amagi Media Labs","portco_name":"Amagi Media Labs","target_website":null,"investor":"Emerald Media","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["Premji Invest","KKR"],"seller":null,"round":"Series D","stake_pct":null,"amount":35000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR-Backed Emerald Media Leads US$35 Million Round in Amagi Media Labs","summary":"KKR-backed Emerald Media acquired a significant minority stake in Amagi Media Labs in a US$35 million Series D.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2dc44a07-af98-49f9-ae16-2ca476057722","evidence":"MUMBAI, DECEMBER 15, 2016: Emerald Media, the Pan-Asia company backed by leading global investment firm KKR for investing in the media and entertainment sector, today announced that it has acquired a significant minority stake in Amagi Media Labs (‘Amagi’), the leader in targeted TV advertising and cloud- based TV broadcast infrastructure. Premji Invest, the investment arm of Azim Premji, (an existing shareholder) is also participating in this combination of primary and secondary US$35 million Series D round.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:4b4e1b420d5b6273dbb9bd67650f64ca","date":"2016-12-13","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Apple Leisure Group","portco_name":"Apple Leisure Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["KSL Capital Partners"],"seller":"Bain Capital Private Equity","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Apple Leisure Group to Be Acquired By KKR and KSL Capital Partners","summary":"KKR and KSL Capital Partners agreed to acquire Apple Leisure Group from Bain Capital; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4ed3dc61-d6be-48bf-8319-084c876723c2","evidence":"PHILADELPHIA--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Apple Leisure Group, a leading hospitality company, today announced that KKR and an affiliate of KSL Capital Partners (KSL) have entered into a definitive agreement to acquire the company from Bain Capital Private Equity. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:06705f20b68bbd99d72ae8a1416c0464","date":"2016-12-08","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"GfK SE","portco_name":"GfK SE","target_website":"gfk.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR To Launch Voluntary Public Tender Offer For GfK SE","summary":"A KKR-controlled holding company announced a voluntary public tender offer for GfK SE at EUR 43.50 per share, with GfK Verein remaining majority shareholder.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a256b7f0-cefc-4866-962a-765bf065a6e3","evidence":"London & Nuremberg, 8 December 2016 – Acceleratio Capital N.V., a holding company controlled by funds advised by Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. L.P. (together with affiliates, “KKR”), today announced its intention to make a voluntary public tender offer for the shares (ISIN: DE0005875306) of GfK SE (“GfK”). The offer price will be EUR 43.50 per share.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:990f00ba3168215c3a23cb3fe45e229d","date":"2016-12-06","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Calvin Capital","portco_name":"Calvin Capital","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Infracapital","round":null,"stake_pct":100.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Infracapital Agrees Sale of Calvin Capital to KKR","summary":"Infracapital agreed to sell 100% of UK smart meter provider Calvin Capital to KKR; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=79c22bd1-20b5-49f1-9ef2-9f449f3ca2c9","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Infracapital, the infrastructure equity investment arm of M&G Investments, announces that it has agreed to sell 100% of the equity of Calvin Capital (“Calvin”), a leading provider of gas and electricity meters to energy suppliers in the UK, to KKR, a leading global investment firm. Financial terms were not disclosed and the transaction is expected to complete at the end of January 2017.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:67de893bcd311daf46bb57ce24ba26c3","date":"2016-12-06","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Optiv","portco_name":"Optiv","target_website":"optiv.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Blackstone","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Optiv Security to Be Acquired By KKR","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in cyber security provider Optiv from private investors including a Blackstone fund.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=82989ad7-553b-4cd5-91a3-f2b2561d369a","evidence":"DENVER & NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Optiv Security, a market-leading provider of end-to-end cyber security solutions, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of a definitive agreement under which KKR will acquire a majority stake in Optiv. The company is being acquired from a group of private investors, including a private equity fund managed by Blackstone (NYSE: BX), which will maintain a minority interest in Optiv along with Optiv management.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b0a20dcee67157dda5a3d43ab5ac4309","date":"2016-11-29","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Hilding Anders","portco_name":"Hilding Anders","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Arle Capital Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires Arle’s Stake in Hilding Anders","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Arle Capital Partners' stake in mattress maker Hilding Anders, becoming majority shareholder.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2ceeb7b0-e2cd-4f83-83ef-5e9ea75f5a68","evidence":"LONDON & MALMÖ, Sweden--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced the signing of an agreement to acquire Arle Capital Partners’ stake in Hilding Anders, subject to regulatory clearances. Following the transaction, KKR will become the majority shareholder in Hilding Anders.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:bc25138a4386afdf428763221b9b127e","date":"2016-11-27","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Capital Juda","portco_name":"Capital Juda","target_website":null,"investor":"Sino-Ocean Group","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":12.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Sino-Ocean and KKR Invest in Capital Juda","summary":"Sino-Ocean and KKR agreed to invest HKD1,477 million in Beijing Capital Juda, with KKR to own about 12%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9f14ddbe-0467-42d3-9822-6fe3bca2d79e","evidence":"HONG KONG--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading Chinese property developer Sino-Ocean Group Holding Limited (“Sino-Ocean”; HKEx: 3377) and global investment firm KKR have entered into a definitive agreement to invest in China leading retail outlets developer and operator Beijing Capital Juda Limited (“Capital Juda” or “The Company”; HKEx: 1329) through a combination of new ordinary shares and perpetual convertible bond securities for a total consideration of HKD1,477 million (US$191 million). Following completion of the transaction, Sino-Ocean will own an approximate 16% stake in Capital Juda and KKR will own an approximate 12% stake in Capital Juda, in each case on a fully diluted basis.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f36314123c44c5d0a1693c0658591dae","date":"2016-11-28","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Exterion Media","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Credit Continues to Extend Sponsor-Led Financing and Direct Lending Activity to Companies","summary":"KKR closed direct lending transactions providing financing for Roompot and Exterion Media.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2e9d333e-88c9-4ad2-8f38-84240c8ae685","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR today announced the closing of two direct lending transactions, which will provide financing for Roompot, a leading operator of holiday parks, and Exterion Media, a leading outdoor advertising company in the UK and Europe.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:04b7c1186c613dea55a7d76345587060","date":"2016-11-22","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Calsonic Kansei","portco_name":"Calsonic Kansei","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Nissan Motor Co., Ltd.","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Tender Offer for the Acquisition of Calsonic Kansei Nissan Agrees to Tender Its 41% Holding of Calsonic Kansei Shares","summary":"A KKR-owned entity announced a tender offer for Calsonic Kansei at JPY 1,860 per share, with Nissan agreeing to tender its 41% holding.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=fe3ecea9-677a-4258-a453-fd9d6ca76f01","evidence":"TOKYO & YOKOHAMA, Japan--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR and Nissan Motor Co., Ltd. (“Nissan”) today announced that CK Holdings Co., Ltd. (the “Bidder”), an entity owned by investment funds controlled by KKR, intends to make a tender offer for all the existing shares of leading Japanese automotive components manufacturer Calsonic Kansei Corporation (“CK” or the “Company”) (Code number: 7248, First Section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange). In connection with the tender offer, the Bidder has entered into a tender agreement (the “Tender Agreement”) with Nissan, the lead shareholder in CK, to acquire in the tender offer Nissan’s approximate 41% holding of CK's common shares. The Bidder plans to pay cash consideration of JPY 1,860 per common share to the existing shareholders of CK.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:71a4226a75c6f84405eb12331e55efb3","date":"2016-11-18","date_text":null,"kind":"secondary","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PHC","portco_name":"PHC","target_website":"phchd.com","investor":"Mitsui & Co., Ltd.","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":22.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Mitsui to Join KKR and Panasonic as an Investor in Panasonic Healthcare","summary":"Mitsui agreed to acquire a 22% stake in KKR-controlled Panasonic Healthcare Holdings (now PHC) for JPY54.1 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4f952a75-2e34-445d-8331-961f83ffec50","evidence":"TOKYO--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Mitsui & Co., Ltd. (“Mitsui”), one of Japan’s largest diversified corporations, and global investment firm KKR today announced the signing of a definitive share purchase agreement for Panasonic Healthcare Holdings (“PHCHD” or “Panasonic Healthcare”), a global provider of healthcare devices. Under the agreement, Mitsui will acquire a 22% stake in PHCHD for JPY54.1 billion (US$510 million). Following the completion of this transaction, KKR will own approximately 58% of PHCHD, Mitsui approximately 22%, and Panasonic Corporation approximately 20%.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7331c8c75d161fb37e7043f2dd6d3ae4","date":"2016-10-19","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"TVS Logistics","portco_name":"TVS Logistics","target_website":null,"investor":"CDPQ","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"Goldman Sachs, KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CDPQ acquires a substantial minority interest in TVS Logistics Services","summary":"CDPQ agreed to invest over INR 1000 crores for a sizeable minority stake in TVS Logistics Services, with Goldman Sachs and KKR fully exiting.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=264d93a9-8bfd-4ea2-b27a-bcb4815be073","evidence":"Under this agreement, CDPQ will invest over INR 1000 crores ($155 million US) to acquire a sizeable minority stake in TVS LSL, a privately held subsidiary of the TVS Group. Following this transaction, existing investors Goldman Sachs and KKR will fully exit their investments in TVS LSL.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:033b15cde3d86f07d40e9620a6f84a2e","date":"2016-10-11","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"YuppTV","portco_name":"YuppTV","target_website":null,"investor":"Emerald Media","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":50000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR-Backed Emerald Media Invests US$50mn in YuppTV","summary":"KKR-backed Emerald Media acquired a significant minority stake in OTT platform YuppTV for US$50mn.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=86b08ee5-4d8f-4d84-ad29-f99481e8d629","evidence":"MUMBAI, INDIA, 11 OCTOBER 2016: Emerald Media, a Pan-Asian platform established by leading global investment firm KKR for investing in the media and entertainment sector today announced that it has acquired a significant minority stake in YuppTV for US$50mn.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8326d88bcb01847ae2b4efef96672d60","date":"2016-10-07","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"OVH","portco_name":"OVH","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["TowerBrook Capital Partners"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":250000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"OVH Partners with KKR and TowerBrook for Further Global Expansion","summary":"KKR and TowerBrook agreed to acquire a minority stake in OVH for €250 million of growth capital.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0e9be6f6-6413-4b58-9fd4-78348a05296b","evidence":"ROUBAIX, France & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- OVH, a leading provider of cloud infrastructure, telecommunications and web hosting services, today finalised a partnership with KKR and TowerBrook Capital Partners (TowerBrook), two leading global investment firms, to further its global expansion. KKR and TowerBrook will acquire a minority stake in OVH for €250 million of growth capital that will allow OVH to take advantage of the rapidly expanding market for cloud and internet infrastructure services, while also broadening its customer base and services in new geographies.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a822ab5b0f6ee9fd15bf5e2e96def3d9","date":"2016-09-09","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"AcuFocus","portco_name":"AcuFocus","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":66000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"AcuFocus Raises $66 Million in New Financing Round Led by KKR","summary":"Ophthalmic device maker AcuFocus raised approximately $66 million in a round led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=df74224e-bc57-41b1-ba7e-2d93c24c46fb","evidence":"IRVINE, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- AcuFocus, Inc., a privately held ophthalmic medical device company, announced today a private investment of approximately $66 million in a financing round led by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:6acc604abd2e9d1eb0f2b5875625171f","date":"2016-08-30","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Calabrio","portco_name":"Calabrio","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire Calabrio, a Global Leader in Customer Engagement and Analytics Software","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire customer engagement software company Calabrio; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1a01b5f2-ffda-4f32-8474-b996881fef0c","evidence":"MINNEAPOLIS, MN -- (Marketwired) -- 08/30/16 -- Calabrio, a leading provider of customer engagement and analytics software, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced today that they have entered into a definitive purchase agreement whereby KKR will acquire Calabrio. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7aaa8a01d3f523c65adf4a018670c6f5","date":"2016-08-04","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"GO-JEK","portco_name":"GO-JEK","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Warburg Pincus","Farallon Capital","Capital Group Private Markets"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":550000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR, Warburg Pincus, Farallon and Capital Group Private Markets Make Substantial Investment in GO-JEK, Indonesia’s Leading On-Demand Mobile Platform","summary":"Indonesia's GO-JEK raised over $550 million from investors including KKR, Warburg Pincus, Farallon and Capital Group Private Markets.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a5dd1ad3-3bb9-4b07-91df-11d328ec9ec2","evidence":"This equity capital raise of over $550 million, which represents the company’s latest round of financing, is comprised of leading investors including KKR, Warburg Pincus, Farallon Capital and Capital Group Private Markets, as well as existing shareholders and other international investors.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:9f5a7673a617dd74e1e9d7323d38c22a","date":"2016-07-28","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Gland Pharma","portco_name":"Gland Pharma","target_website":null,"investor":"Fosun Pharma","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":86.0,"amount":1260000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Gland Pharma to be Acquired by Fosun Pharma","summary":"Fosun Pharma agreed to acquire about 86% of Gland Pharma for up to US$1.26 billion, with KKR divesting its full stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3ef64d15-c106-4dad-a0c4-405a55074674","evidence":"KKR to Divest its Full Stake HYDERABAD--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Gland Pharma Limited (“Gland” or “The Company”), a leading Indian pure-play generic injectable pharmaceutical products company, today announced the signing of a definitive agreement under which Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical (Group) Co. Ltd. (together with its subsidiaries, “Fosun Pharma”), a leading Chinese health care provider (stock code: 600196.SH,02196.HK), will acquire an approximate 86% stake in Gland for up to US$1.26 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:5a06bc63f0f6fed4bcbda3ab4f386037","date":"2016-07-11","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"UFC","portco_name":"UFC","target_website":null,"investor":"WME | IMG","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["Silver Lake Partners","KKR","MSD Capital"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"WME | IMG To Acquire UFC®","summary":"WME | IMG announced the acquisition of UFC, with Silver Lake and KKR joining as new strategic investors and KKR Capital Markets among financing providers.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=cc46b275-562b-4661-9366-b6edf959bdd2","evidence":"BEVERLY HILLS, Calif., July 11, 2016 /PRNewswire/ -- WME | IMG today announced the acquisition of UFC, the world's premier professional mixed martial arts (MMA) organization. Silver Lake Partners and KKR will join WME | IMG as new strategic investors, along with MSD Capital, L.P. and MSD Partners, L.P. which will provide preferred equity financing.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4590b1c6c3e97e66806d6f48db7e4226","date":"2016-07-05","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Epicor Software","portco_name":"Epicor Software","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Apax Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Epicor Growth Strategy Affirmed With Acquisition by Leading Global Investment Firm KKR","summary":"Epicor agreed to be acquired by KKR from funds advised by Apax Partners; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2293d446-a7fd-4319-af52-baaf52177de7","evidence":"AUSTIN, TX -- (Marketwired) -- 07/05/16 -- Epicor Software Corporation, a global provider of industry-specific enterprise software to promote business growth, announced today that it has entered into a definitive agreement to be acquired by the global investment firm KKR from funds advised by Apax Partners.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:027bc829878950f23dcf5bd86ba12cbf","date":"2016-06-27","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Resource Environmental Solutions (\"RES\")","portco_name":"Resource Environmental Solutions (\"RES\")","target_website":"res.us","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Resource Environmental Solutions Receives Investment from KKR","summary":"KKR made a significant investment in ecological restoration company RES.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=50e2fd57-328c-45d7-a69e-0124c24e9e79","evidence":"HOUSTON & NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Resource Environmental Solutions, LLC (“RES”), a leader in the ecological solutions market, today announced that global investment firm KKR is making a significant investment in RES to support its next phase of growth and development.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:dafd2fecd221ee554d15f963c356c09a","date":"2016-06-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Coriance","portco_name":"Coriance","target_website":null,"investor":"First State Investments","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"First State Investments Acquires Coriance from KKR","summary":"First State Investments agreed to acquire French district heating company Coriance from KKR's infrastructure funds and a co-investor.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=15491a4e-ba29-4aba-b91c-dd38c02784a8","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- First State Investments and KKR have entered into an agreement by which Coriance, a French district heating company which is currently owned by KKR’s infrastructure funds and a co-investor, will be acquired by First State Investments managed infrastructure funds.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:fb22d52dade0dadc9c8d0c71b317fc38","date":"2016-06-08","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PT Japfa Tbk","portco_name":"PT Japfa Tbk","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Japfa","round":null,"stake_pct":10.44,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Will Invest US$81.2 Million1 for a 10.44% Interest in PT Japfa Tbk","summary":"KKR agreed to invest about US$81.2 million for a 10.44% interest in PT Japfa Tbk through a private placement and a share purchase from Japfa.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9eb8bc9d-f36d-41d5-a767-e3b3591337a0","evidence":"KKR Will Invest US$81.2 Million1 for a 10.44% Interest in PT Japfa Tbk PT Japfa Tbk will place out 750.0 million new shares to KKR via a private placement at approximately US$52.9 million1. Concurrent with the private placement, Japfa will sell 441.7 million shares in PT Japfa Tbk to KKR for an estimated sum of US$28.3 million1.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:59cda778cd991c65712dbbeff3d8dd59","date":"2016-05-17","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Pillarstone","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Alpha Bank","Eurobank"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Alpha Bank, Eurobank and KKR Reach Agreement to Support Greek Companies","summary":"Alpha Bank, Eurobank and KKR Credit agreed to assign management of exposures to selected Greek companies to the Pillarstone platform.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d4efc6a7-2404-433f-aa16-b45ee9c91949","evidence":"ATHENS, Greece--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Alpha Bank, Eurobank and KKR Credit have reached a binding agreement today by which the banks agree to assign the management of credit and equity exposures to a selected number of Greek companies into a platform managed by Pillarstone.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:e786e55f7db608f24ab4f924b938efc1","date":"2016-04-11","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ticket Monster","portco_name":"Ticket Monster","target_website":null,"investor":"NHN Entertainment","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":40000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":1500000000.0,"valuation_currency":"USD","headline":"KKR-backed Ticket Monster receives investment from NHN Entertainment","summary":"NHN Entertainment completed a US$40 million investment in KKR-backed Ticket Monster, valuing it at US$1.5 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0cbe8b8b-191c-4466-9cc8-e78101a46ff8","evidence":"SEOUL – April 11, 2016 – Leading South Korean mobile commerce company Ticket Monster (“TMON”) today announced that NHN Entertainment (“NHNE”), Korea’s premiere gaming and entertainment provider, has completed a US$40 million (KRW 47.5 billion) investment in the company. NHNE’s investment valued TMON at US$1.5 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:7785d281f3f3ef90a6be7bca9cb76550","date":"2016-03-31","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"SMCP Group","portco_name":"SMCP Group","target_website":null,"investor":"Shandong Ruyi Technology Group","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Shandong Ruyi Technology Group Enters into Exclusivity Agreement with a View to Acquiring a Majority Stake in SMCP Group","summary":"KKR and SMCP management entered exclusivity for Shandong Ruyi Group to acquire a controlling stake in SMCP, with KKR retaining a minority interest.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=a9d399ce-2a57-495c-93b3-7e4c35a406f2","evidence":"PARIS, LONDON & JINING, China--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Shandong Ruyi Technology Group (\"Shandong Ruyi Group\") and KKR, a leading global investment firm, together with the founders and management team of SMCP Group (“SMCP”) have today announced the signing of an exclusivity agreement for the acquisition of a controlling stake in SMCP by Shandong Ruyi Group. The parties contemplate that SMCP’s founders and management would reinvest alongside Shandong Ruyi Group as minority shareholders, while KKR would retain a minority interest in the group.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:ac97dd050096ec7611826a908cf75558","date":"2016-03-30","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Scout24 Schweiz","portco_name":"Scout24 Schweiz","target_website":null,"investor":"Swiss Mobiliar","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":50.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Swiss Mobiliar Agrees to Acquire KKR’s Stake in Scout24 Schweiz and Becomes New Shareholder alongside Ringier","summary":"Swiss Mobiliar agreed to acquire the 50% stake in Scout24 Schweiz held by KKR and other shareholders, joining Ringier.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=be6b3aee-bd04-4a99-8e76-c4aba4e0b05c","evidence":"ZURICH--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Ringier AG (Ringier), the largest international media company in Switzerland, and Swiss Mobiliar, the country’s oldest private insurance company, have agreed to form a strategic partnership whereby Swiss Mobiliar will become the new joint shareholder in Scout24 Schweiz AG (Scout24 Schweiz), the leading network of online marketplaces for motor vehicles, real estate and general classifieds. Swiss Mobiliar will acquire a fifty per cent stake in Scout24 Schweiz, previously held by KKR and other shareholders, in spring 2016. KKR, a leading global investment firm, acquired its stake in Scout24 Schweiz in August 2014.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:78090b32f610abd47f0bc1735afb6e2b","date":"2016-03-28","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Yiguo","portco_name":"Yiguo","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Alibaba"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Yiguo completes largest fundraising round in China's fresh food e-commerce sector","summary":"Chinese fresh food e-commerce platform Yiguo completed a Series C from investors including KKR and Alibaba.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c7f47840-53a2-4337-aee5-00a84aa1f566","evidence":"SHANGHAI – March 28, 2016 – Yiguo, a leading fresh food e-commerce platform in China, today announced that it has completed a Series C financing from investors including global investment firm KKR and the company's existing shareholder and strategic partner Alibaba. Specific details of the transaction are not being disclosed, but the financing is recognized as China's largest fresh-food e-commerce fundraise, according to sources such as CVSource and Zero2IPO.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:300c1cb0653b358842934ee87dc0bfcc","date":"2016-03-15","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Spirox","portco_name":"Spirox","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["HealthQuest Capital","Aisling Capital","Aperture Venture Partners","Venrock"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":45000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Spirox, Inc. Announces Closing of $45MM Series C Financing","summary":"Medical device company Spirox closed a $45 million Series C led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=5c60543a-4c91-4e5f-9c6f-19b4d338fb34","evidence":"MENLO PARK, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Spirox Inc., a privately held medical device company, announced today the closing of a $45 million Series C round of financing led by KKR, a leading global investment firm. In leading the round, KKR joins a strong syndicate of existing investors in the company.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:3eb48a24394c5fc3aa8c8bebd2e1ecad","date":"2016-02-23","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Chesapeake non-operated royalty portfolio","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Haymaker Resources","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":"Chesapeake Energy Corporation","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":128000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Haymaker Acquires a Portion of Chesapeake’s Non-Operated Royalty Portfolio for $128 Million","summary":"KKR-backed Haymaker Resources acquired a portion of Chesapeake's non-operated royalty portfolio for $128 million.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b82670a9-7c5a-4a89-81d9-7f241682814a","evidence":"Haymaker Acquires a Portion of Chesapeake’s Non-Operated Royalty Portfolio for $128 Million HOUSTON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- On January 29, 2016, Houston-based Haymaker Resources closed on the acquisition of mineral and royalty interests from certain affiliates of Oklahoma City-based Chesapeake Energy Corporation.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:9058acf9234667b2bc1fc16ec428a2bd","date":"2016-02-17","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Max Financial Services","portco_name":"Max Financial Services","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":9.95,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Max Financial Services","summary":"KKR acquired an approximate 9.95% stake in Max Financial Services from a sponsor group led by Analjit Singh.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=042cdf06-1f95-402d-8cc9-c9760a298b29","evidence":"MUMBAI, India--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR today announced that it has acquired an approximate 9.95% stake in Max Financial Services (BSE:500271), the newly demerged entity of the Max Group that owns an approximate 72% stake in Max Life, India’s fourth-largest private life insurance player. KKR acquired its stake from a sponsor group led by Analjit Singh, Chairman Emeritus of the Max Group.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:cfd1c05cde5955df188ae77552b8831f","date":"2016-02-10","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"A10 Capital","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":75000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"A10 Capital Closes $75 Million Investment Facility From KKR","summary":"Commercial real estate lender A10 Capital closed a $75 million investment facility from KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ad50b8b7-e0da-47c3-8064-6d3a93f73efc","evidence":"BOISE, ID -- (Marketwired) -- 02/10/16 -- A10 Capital, the nation's leading middle-market commercial real estate lender, today announced it closed a $75 million investment facility from KKR.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:72e63d00a88387925bc8bfbbb2cdbd37","date":"2016-02-09","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Välinge Group","portco_name":"Välinge Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Kronospan, Swiss Krono Group, Pervan family","round":null,"stake_pct":50.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Entrepreneurial Family Owner Pervan Partners with KKR","summary":"KKR signed agreements to acquire a combined 50% stake in Swedish R&D company Välinge from Kronospan, Swiss Krono and the founder.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b8e0405b-6b36-4a6b-bdc8-f6eced9b21b4","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investor, has today announced the signing of three agreements to ultimately acquire a combined 50% stake in Välinge, a Swedish industrial R&D company founded and owned by the Pervan family. Through the agreements, KKR will acquire the two 20% stakes of the current minority owners, Kronospan and Swiss Krono Group, as well as an additional 10% stake from the founder.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7374cc711394d3fd8dca2d1e1d8b2222","date":"2016-02-03","date_text":null,"kind":"secondary","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"South Staffordshire Plc","portco_name":"South Staffordshire","target_website":null,"investor":"Mitsubishi Corporation","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":25.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR agrees the sale of a 25% stake in South Staffordshire Plc to Mitsubishi Corporation","summary":"KKR agreed to sell a 25% stake in South Staffordshire Plc to Mitsubishi Corporation.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=88ce7362-c60e-4670-8b05-b3d1b84ea812","evidence":"London, 03 February 2016 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Mitsubishi Corporation (MC), a global integrated trading company which develops and operates businesses across a variety of industries, entered into an agreement by which a 25% stake in South Staffordshire Plc, currently owned and controlled by KKR’s infrastructure funds and other accounts, will be sold to MC.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:62c8f1b13ec20cf274370c40c68e4a91","date":"2016-01-28","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Masan Consumer","portco_name":"Masan Consumer","target_website":null,"investor":"Masan Group","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Masan Group Conclude Successful Partnership in Masan Consumer","summary":"KKR concluded its partnership in Masan Consumer as Masan Group purchased the remainder of KKR's equity, after KKR invested $159 million in 2011 and $200 million in 2013.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=fe35c726-750c-4ae8-b3b9-5644db2e0dfb","evidence":"SINGAPORE--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR today announced that it has concluded its partnership with Masan Group Corporation (HOSE:MSN, “Masan”) as Masan purchased the remainder of KKR’s equity in Masan Consumer Corporation (\"Masan Consumer\"), Vietnam’s leading diversified branded food and beverage company. KKR first invested $159 million in Masan Consumer in 2011 with a second follow-on investment of $200 million in 2013, making it the largest private equity investment in Vietnam.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:01bff11cff4202fe14b9832d3e5814a3","date":"2016-01-26","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Jitterbit","portco_name":"Jitterbit","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":"Series B","stake_pct":null,"amount":20000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Jitterbit Raises $20 Million in Series B Funding Round Led by KKR to Expand Jitterbit's Market-Leading Cloud Integration Platform","summary":"Jitterbit raised a $20 million Series B led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b92ba143-3f45-40f7-8141-4be5f8e638d9","evidence":"ALAMEDA, CA -- (Marketwired) -- 01/26/16 -- Jitterbit, the leading provider of fast, agile integration solutions for the modern business, today announced that it has raised $20 million in a Series B round led by the global investment firm KKR.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:f67cad8febcfc3060181e3d47080537c","date":"2016-01-15","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"GE Appliances","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Qingdao Haier","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":"General Electric","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":5400000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Haier Group Enters into MoU for Global Strategic Partnership with General Electric","summary":"Qingdao Haier, 50.8% owned by Haier Group and KKR together, agreed to acquire GE Appliances for $5.4 billion cash consideration.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=dbea22a6-ff0c-40ef-a5fd-fc2b58098e61","evidence":"In addition, Qingdao Haier Co., Ltd. (SHA: 600690; “Qingdao Haier”), a Shanghai stock exchange listed company that is 41% owned by Haier, will acquire the GE Appliances business (“GE Appliances”). As part of the acquisition, GE will receive a cash consideration from Qingdao Haier of $5.4 billion. Haier Group and KKR, who together own 50.8% of Qingdao Haier shares outstanding, are fully supportive of the transaction.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:b504ed9c3378a7101e7e6754be13c8ea","date":"2016-01-05","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Mills Fleet Farm","portco_name":"Mills Fleet Farm","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Mills Fleet Farm Announces New Ownership to Carry on Founders’ Vision of Honesty, Integrity, Value and Service","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Midwestern retailer Mills Fleet Farm from the founding Mills family.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=79ded5bf-74e8-4493-91b7-585dae99f1f3","evidence":"APPLETON, Wis. & BRAINERD, Minn.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Mills Fleet Farm, a Midwestern, value-based retailer of lifestyle merchandise serving active outdoor families as well as suburban and farm consumers, and KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced today that they have entered into a definitive purchase agreement where KKR will acquire Mills Fleet Farm.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:42366b6ef5f36f942548c436ce2a8343","date":"2026-02-18","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Accell Group","portco_name":"Accell Group","target_website":null,"investor":"Undisclosed","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Statement on Accell Group Ownership Transition","summary":"Accell Group, its shareholders and lenders agreed a new ownership structure led by the company's existing lenders, ending KKR's ownership after the e-bike downturn.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=73d8f231-14d3-4d85-b7ee-75685cef48d1","evidence":"Following constructive engagement, Accell Group, its shareholders and lenders have now agreed to a new ownership structure led by the company’s existing lenders to support the business in its next phase. With the company now stabilised and the season soon to pick up, Accell will transition to a new ownership structure in which lenders, working closely with management, are positioned to support the company’s ongoing recovery and execution of its business plan.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:dfa9e3fc98c6fdd1313fe4b0493f5adf","date":"2025-04-09","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Karo Healthcare","portco_name":"Karo Healthcare","target_website":"karohealthcare.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"EQT","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Karo Healthcare announces KKR as new owner, following successful strategic transformation into pan-European consumer healthcare player","summary":"EQT agreed to sell pan-European consumer healthcare company Karo Healthcare to KKR funds.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=7ecc4159-5c35-4da0-b794-ae0027659b8f","evidence":"Karo Healthcare (“Karo”) will change owner following the announcement that EQT has agreed to sell Karo to funds managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f75fe5ded6ecb284353f28d719e05759","date":"2024-10-28","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Superstruct Entertainment","portco_name":"Superstruct Entertainment","target_website":"superstruct.com","investor":"CVC","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC joins KKR in the acquisition of Superstruct Entertainment","summary":"CVC invested alongside KKR in festival operator Superstruct Entertainment following KKR's June 2024 acquisition.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d3c327f2-83d8-449a-b732-49885585be2f","evidence":"London, October 28, 2024 – KKR and CVC, two leading global investment firms, today announce that CVC has invested alongside KKR to support Superstruct Entertainment (“Superstruct”) in its next phase of development as one of the world’s premier live entertainment groups. In June 2024, KKR announced the acquisition of Superstruct, which owns and operates over 80 music festivals across 10 countries in Europe and Australia.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5b10feab179acf973f629e00095b7e6c","date":"2024-04-29","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Leonine","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Mediawan","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","Atwater Capital"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"MEDIAWAN ANNOUNCES COMBINATION WITH LEONINE, ONE OF THE LARGEST INDEPENDENT STUDIOS IN THE GERMAN-SPEAKING MARKET","summary":"KKR-backed Mediawan announced a combination with KKR-backed German studio Leonine.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=7f6d658b-fab5-4e7c-8215-fdd683bfccb3","evidence":"Leonine was founded in 2019 by Fred Kogel and his management team with financial support from KKR[1] and Atwater Capital[1] through acquiring and merging TMG, Universum Film, i&u TV and Wiedemann & Berg Film, followed by W&B Television, SEO Entertainment, hyperbole, BeetzBros Film Production and Toon2Tango. Mediawan is controlled by its co-founders Pierre-Antoine Capton, Xavier Niel and Matthieu Pigasse, with financial backing from KKR[1] and other long-term partners. KKR’s investments in Mediawan and Leonine follow a long history of investing behind exceptional entrepreneurs in talent - and IP - centred businesses.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:082151fa143bf3421c49fa118cbec3e6","date":"2022-10-21","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Advanta Seeds","portco_name":"Advanta Seeds","target_website":"advantaseeds.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"UPL Limited","round":null,"stake_pct":13.33,"amount":300000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Joins UPL as an Investor in Advanta","summary":"KKR agreed to invest US$300 million for a 13.33% stake in UPL's seed subsidiary Advanta Enterprises.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=73261896-bb97-461e-a291-1b7af1d445ac","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and UPL Limited (“UPL”), a global agriculture solutions provider, today announced the signing of definitive agreements under which KKR will invest US$300 million for a 13.33% stake in Advanta Enterprises Limited (“Advanta” or “the Company”), a subsidiary of UPL and a leading global seed company that aims to deliver innovative farming solutions and technology to farmers around the world.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:364876a680dd85f25934c0ae54d72fc9","date":"2021-12-09","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"GreenCollar","portco_name":"GreenCollar","target_website":null,"investor":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ontario Teachers’ Joins KKR as an Investor in GreenCollar","summary":"Ontario Teachers' joined KKR's Global Impact Fund as a significant shareholder in GreenCollar.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=bdb33c02-3dba-4c25-bba9-c2e9f1e710d2","evidence":"GreenCollar is pleased to welcome Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan Board (Ontario Teachers’) as a new long-term investor to back the company’s ambitious growth aspirations and commitment to delivering positive environmental impact at scale. With this latest investment, Ontario Teachers’ joins KKR’s Global Impact Fund as a significant shareholder in the company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:244156b235d8008abe776db6c29d0a94","date":"2021-12-09","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Malteries Soufflet","portco_name":"Malteries Soufflet","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Bpifrance","Crédit Agricole Group"],"seller":"InVivo Group","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":440000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR joins InVivo in its acquisition of global malt producer Malteries Soufflet","summary":"KKR acquired a significant minority stake in malt producer Malteries Soufflet, investing with Bpifrance and Crédit Agricole a total of €440m alongside InVivo.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2cfe6be1-9ccf-482f-a567-f997a0c833f9","evidence":"KKR is co-investing with Bpifrance and Crédit Agricole Group for a total consideration of €440m Paris, 9 December, 2021 – KKR, a leading global investment firm, announces today that KKR has acquired a significant minority stake in Malteries Soufflet, a leading producer in the malt industry. KKR, Bpifrance and Crédit Agricole Group will collectively invest €440m in the malt business, which is a division of Soufflet Group.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:e7468fab20116d3c916f3e49581646e2","date":"2021-09-07","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"RainFocus","portco_name":"RainFocus","target_website":"rainfocus.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["JMI Equity"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"RainFocus Closes Series C Funding Round Led by KKR","summary":"Event marketing platform RainFocus closed a Series C led by KKR with JMI Equity participating.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8d1436f8-5542-42c3-aedd-8bd4251b3116","evidence":"Lehi, UT, Sept. 07, 2021 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- RainFocus, the next-generation enterprise event marketing platform, today announced that it has closed its Series C funding round led by KKR, a leading global investment firm. Existing investor JMI Equity, a growth equity firm focused on investing in leading software companies, also participated in the round.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:a0c23e9bb627b2e7b32c011ebb407982","date":"2019-07-10","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Webhelp","portco_name":"Webhelp","target_website":null,"investor":"Groupe Bruxelles Lambert","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2400000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Enters Exclusive Negotiations with GBL for Webhelp Group","summary":"KKR entered exclusive negotiations to sell a majority stake in Webhelp to GBL on the basis of an enterprise value of €2.4 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=195663b8-c0f9-48b1-a020-e76dbe77382d","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, announces today it has entered into exclusive negotiations to sell a majority stake in the Webhelp group to Groupe Bruxelles Lambert (\"GBL\"). As a result of this transaction, GBL would acquire a majority stake in Webhelp on the basis of an enterprise value of €2.4 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:229767dab51b1571768a9d0763d48821","date":"2017-10-25","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"PT Nippon Indosari Corpindo","portco_name":"PT Nippon Indosari Corpindo","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":12.64,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Becomes Shareholder of PT Nippon Indosari Corpindo Tbk.","summary":"KKR acquired an approximate 12.64% stake in Indonesian bread maker Nippon Indosari Corpindo from its Asian Fund III.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0a0c545c-84b5-46e1-b7b0-4f6c5b061996","evidence":"JAKARTA, Indonesia--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR today announced that KKR has acquired an approximate 12.64% stake in PT Nippon Indosari Corpindo Tbk. (\"Indosari\" or the \"Company\") (IDX stock code: ROTI), Indonesia’s leading mass market bread company. KKR makes its investment from its Asian Fund III.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5b9e8aab0b882210d64f5ef8fdd53a65","date":"2017-05-12","date_text":null,"kind":"ipo","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Gardner Denver","portco_name":"Gardner Denver","target_website":null,"investor":"Undisclosed","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Gardner Denver Marks First Day of Trading on New York Stock Exchange by Announcing More Than $100 Million in Equity Grants to Global Workforce","summary":"KKR-majority-owned Gardner Denver listed on the New York Stock Exchange in its initial public offering.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3b24e399-0384-40d0-8f6f-819acad1397d","evidence":"In a video message seen worldwide, GDI and majority owner KKR tell nearly 6,000 employees they will become stockholders In a video message to team members around the globe, Vicente Reynal, Gardner Denver CEO, and Pete Stavros, Gardner Denver Board Chairman and KKR Member and Head of its Industrials Private Equity Team, announced that in conjunction with the company's initial public offering, each employee not already part of the company's equity program - from hourly production to customer service to sales personnel - will receive a significant grant of company stock (in the form of deferred stock units).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:d2bc3e3f2e6d4d6439942b974655524f","date":"2017-05-02","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ajax Health","portco_name":"Ajax Health","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Aisling Capital"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Ajax Health Formed to Help Address Unmet Needs in the Medical Device Field","summary":"KKR and Aisling Capital created medical device platform Ajax Health under Duke Rohlen.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=14955a6d-3e3f-4059-9f63-44fb1cec2078","evidence":"MENLO PARK, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, along with Aisling Capital, today announced the creation of a new platform, Ajax Health (“Ajax”), which will source and provide operational and financial capabilities to a diversified portfolio of emerging medical device companies under the leadership of Duke Rohlen.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:21c0e109d43789d7a1567be31c5631f8","date":"2017-04-02","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Masan Group","portco_name":"Masan Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"PENM Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":250000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Backs Masan Group to be Vietnam’s Future Consumer Champion","summary":"KKR agreed to invest US$250 million in Masan Group, including US$100 million of secondary shares and US$150 million for 7.5% of Masan Nutri-Science.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b7645336-e3d6-4008-a683-47ea9ebfa311","evidence":"HO CHI MINH CITY, Vietnam & SINGAPORE--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Masan Group Corporation (HOSE:MSN, “Masan Group” and the “Company”), today announced that KKR, a leading global investment firm, has entered into definitive agreements to invest a total of US$250 million in Masan Group and in its branded meat platform, Masan Nutri-Science (the “Transaction”). KKR’s investment is comprised of a US$100 million purchase of secondary shares of Masan Group from PENM Partners, an independent Danish private equity company, and a US$150 million primary investment in Masan Nutri-Science for a 7.5% stake.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0a89dcd54337f19f966a7c9146235152","date":"2016-07-06","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Darktrace","portco_name":"Darktrace","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Summit Partners","TenEleven Ventures","SB ISAT Fund"],"seller":null,"round":"growth","stake_pct":null,"amount":65000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cyber Security Company Darktrace in $65 Million Fundraise to Accelerate Global Expansion in Round Led by KKR","summary":"Darktrace raised $65 million in growth equity financing led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=61d256bd-a8c5-4927-b8cf-092ed12e677f","evidence":"Cyber Security Company Darktrace in $65 Million Fundraise to Accelerate Global Expansion in Round Led by KKR SAN FRANCISCO & CAMBRIDGE, England--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Darktrace, a provider of enterprise cyber threat defense software, announced today that it has raised new growth equity financing, led by KKR, a leading global investment firm, with participation from existing investor Summit Partners, and new investors TenEleven Ventures and SoftBank-affiliated SB ISAT Fund.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:c4b28a4f8f11450cb6482d7cb2ce2e65","date":"2026-03-20","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Pepper Money UK","portco_name":"Pepper Group","target_website":null,"investor":"Bayview","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Pepper Money UK announces transition to standalone UK-regulated entity","summary":"Pepper Money UK became a standalone UK-regulated entity in a transaction including new equity from a Bayview fund alongside KKR private credit funds.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d248ed58-15cc-44bf-ad82-bf4f46c8b879","evidence":"Pepper Money UK, a leading specialist mortgage lender, today announces its transition to operating as a standalone UK-regulated entity, following the receipt in December 2025 of the Financial Conduct Authority’s (FCA) approval of the change in regulatory control. The transaction includes a new equity commitment by a fund managed by Bayview alongside private credit funds and accounts managed or advised by KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:e80cd98110d80d058e0c84feaa8a02bd","date":"2023-12-07","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Smart Metering Systems plc","portco_name":"Smart Metering Systems plc","target_website":"sms-plc.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1400000000.0,"currency":"GBP","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Recommended acquisition of Smart Metering Systems plc","summary":"A KKR-backed bidco agreed a recommended all-cash acquisition of Smart Metering Systems at 955 pence per share, valuing its equity at about £1.3 billion and implying an enterprise value of about £1.4 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4d528d76-1c3d-4ed5-8a5b-713c0dc66893","evidence":"The Acquisition values the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of SMS at approximately £1.3 billion on a fully diluted basis, and this implies an enterprise value of approximately £1.4 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a1568db33479f8d48e4247752e373e9a","date":"2025-09-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Sempra Infrastructure Partners","portco_name":"Sempra Infrastructure","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponso