amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"State Bank of India approves sale of 3.9% stake in SBI Life to KKR and Temasek","summary":"State Bank of India approved the sale of a 3.9% stake in SBI Life to KKR and Temasek.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=120994be-1a7c-4a64-b102-2c0f5861f237","evidence":"State Bank of India approves sale of 3.9% stake in SBI Life to KKR and Temasek","verified":null},{"key":"pr:17d2f050bfc515079555ce7185de8078","date":"2021-04-07","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Open Dutch Fiber","portco_name":"Open Dutch Fiber","target_website":"opendutchfiber.nl","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["DTCP"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":700000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"unspecified","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and DTCP Roll Out Fiber Infrastructure in the Netherlands","summary":"KKR and DTCP launched Dutch open access fiber platform Open Dutch Fiber with a fully funded commitment for envisaged capital expenditure of about €700 million.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=3f08fd1d-45d5-4f8e-93e6-df649c9fd1d2","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, and DTCP, an investment management platform focusing on digital infrastructure and growth equity, today announced the launch of Open Dutch Fiber and a strategic agreement between Open Dutch Fiber and T-Mobile Netherlands. Open Dutch Fiber will begin operations in Q2 2021 with a fully-funded commitment for an envisaged capital expenditure of approximately €700 million and construction agreements already in place.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:74117b4450681c72c8b1e8caf29a1cf8","date":"2021-03-01","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Caruna Oy","portco_name":"Caruna Oy","target_website":"caruna.fi","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board"],"seller":"First Sentier Investors, OMERS","round":null,"stake_pct":20.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"AMF, Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan Board and KKR become new shareholders in Caruna alongside Elo","summary":"Ontario Teachers' and KKR each acquired 20% of Finnish electricity distributor Caruna from First Sentier and agreed to buy a further 40% from OMERS, taking each to 40%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=547d82df-833c-41be-a1ac-078279d96568","evidence":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board (Ontario Teachers’) and KKR have each acquired a 20% holding in Caruna, Finland’s largest electricity distribution company, from First Sentier Investors (FSI). Separately, Ontario Teachers’ and KKR have signed binding documentation to acquire a further 40% holding in Caruna from OMERS, which will increase their ownership to 40% each.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:16f7baa0904b8188ad186b8b24dba22d","date":"2020-05-12","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"My Pizza Technologies, Inc.","portco_name":"My Pizza Technologies, Inc.","target_website":"slicelife.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["GGV Capital"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":43000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Slice Closes $43 Million in Series C Funding Led by KKR","summary":"Pizzeria ordering platform Slice raised $43 million in a Series C led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8826fd6c-4b79-417f-b2a9-b71ff71a21fa","evidence":"NEW YORK--Slice, the all-in-one ordering and marketing tech platform for local pizzerias, today announced that it has raised $43 million in Series C funding. KKR led the round with participation from existing early investors, including GGV Capital.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:7f5e2076536624d7ed27e8862b6d4558","date":"2019-04-08","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Wiedemann & Berg Film","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Tele München Gruppe","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","Atwater Capital, LLC"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Fred Kogel, Max Wiedemann and Quirin Berg to create independent German media company","summary":"Wiedemann & Berg Film joined the KKR-backed independent German media company with Tele München Gruppe, Universum Film and i&u TV (later Leonine).","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2032b26c-2b92-4f00-af78-d0338597fab2","evidence":"Wiedemann & Berg Film, one of the most successful German film production companies, to complement Tele München Gruppe, Universum Film and i&u TV W&B Film will become a part of the independent media company backed by KKR, with the participation of Atwater Capital, LLC. KKR is making its investment from its European Fund IV.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:aaf1236fd58885110096a6b1cc2270db","date":"2017-08-07","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"URSA","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Xella International GmbH","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"URSA Becomes Part of the Xella Portfolio","summary":"Xella International acquired insulation maker URSA from shareholders including majority owner KKR funds; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=98776092-641e-49af-b50a-6d0f3c789bca","evidence":"MADRID & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Xella International GmbH, a leading European building materials provider, announced the acquisition of URSA from its shareholders, including funds managed by KKR as majority owners. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7fb6afc080f029e4a581716d5258031f","date":"2016-02-03","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Sunteck Realty","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Fund Sunteck Realty's Flagship Residential Project in Mumbai","summary":"KKR's investment vehicles agreed to provide up to Rs150 crore (US$22.4 million) of funding to Sunteck Realty's flagship Mumbai residential developments.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b6596d15-9fbc-40fb-9518-42d69fe12775","evidence":"MUMBAI - February 3, 2016 - Sunteck Realty Ltd., A Mumbai-based premium real estate developer, today announced the signing of a definitive agreement with leading global investment firm KKR under which KKR's investment vehicles would provide up to Rs150 crore (US$22.4 million) of funding to Sunteck's flagship luxury residential developments in Mumbai, Signia Isles and Signia Pearl.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:035270d1e20317f1013837d7e50272ba","date":"2024-10-31","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Birch Creek Energy","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":150000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Birch Creek Closes $150m Credit Facility with KKR","summary":"Solar developer Birch Creek closed a $150 million credit facility from KKR insurance accounts within its High-Grade ABF strategy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b151c65f-cd84-4f2b-a3f7-e2c4d52343fc","evidence":"LOUIS, Oct. 31, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Birch Creek Energy, LLC (\"Birch Creek\"), a utility scale solar and storage developer and independent power producer, and KKR, a leading global investment ﬁrm, today announced that Birch Creek has closed on a $150 million credit facility within KKR's High-Grade Asset-Based Finance (ABF) strategy via insurance accounts managed by KKR.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:cac78100e29627214795bba4f20118ae","date":"2024-10-02","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Powin","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":200000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Powin Secures $200 Million in Debt Capital From KKR to Bolster Growth and Innovation in Energy Storage","summary":"Energy storage provider Powin secured a revolving credit facility of up to $200 million primarily from KKR-managed insurance accounts.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=6c7027f8-8c84-4d24-9f9d-349539de2512","evidence":"PORTLAND, Ore.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Powin, a global leader in battery energy storage solutions, announced today that it has successfully secured a revolving credit facility of up to $200 million primarily from insurance accounts managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:c018e6be292990fe8e67b9e63ce2f0b2","date":"2024-05-20","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Origis Energy","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":300000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Provides $300 Million Corporate Credit Facility to Origis Energy","summary":"KKR's insurance business provided a $300 million corporate financing facility to renewable energy platform Origis Energy.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=117490e3-45d1-489b-87d3-c302bb734049","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm and Origis Energy (“Origis”), a leading renewable energy and decarbonization solution platform, today announced that vehicles and accounts managed by KKR’s insurance business have provided a $300 million corporate financing facility to Origis.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0f7f1976a6f7fd7b054940118a720e64","date":"2024-01-22","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Weber LLC","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":200000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Provides Global Accounts Receivable Facility to Weber LLC","summary":"KKR private credit funds provided Weber an initial $200 million non-recourse accounts receivable facility, with up to $100 million more expected in Europe.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f414361b-6b26-4bfc-921a-e70c3526504c","evidence":"KKR today announced that its private credit funds and accounts have provided a non-recourse accounts receivable financing for Weber LLC (“Weber”), the global leader in outdoor cooking products, innovation, and technology, to support the company’s operations and strategic investments in long-term growth. The initial $200 million facility is collateralized by certain accounts receivables of Weber in the U.S. and international markets, with subsequent closes of up to $100 million across European markets expected in the first half of 2024.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:435451a0de4c7f668fc1cd66d24c6e52","date":"2023-09-15","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"REVEL","portco_name":"REVEL","target_website":null,"investor":"Undisclosed","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["Santander Consumer Finance","KKR"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":115000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"REVEL secures €115 million to boost its car subscription business in Spain","summary":"Spanish car subscription company REVEL completed a €115 million transaction of €15 million equity and up to €100 million debt financing structured with KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1d49cc55-b182-4026-bb7b-dc774b716321","evidence":"● The funding round, which consists of an equity investment in the company of €15 million and a structured financing of €100 million, has been participated in by Santander Consumer Finance and KKR, among others. Madrid, 15th September, 2023 – REVEL, a Spanish company specializing in digital car subscription services, has successfully completed a transaction totaling €115 million.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:a7040b52b83d29298b7e4ace3003e288","date":"2022-10-20","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Flexport Capital","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":200000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Flexport Capital Secures $200 Million Credit Facility from KKR","summary":"Flexport Capital secured a $200 million credit facility from KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=10fab692-3049-44aa-96e3-5f8536efe804","evidence":"Flexport Capital Secures $200 Million Credit Facility from KKR","verified":true},{"key":"pr:095e0c868dbe82eecebe0f2fe87314bb","date":"2022-08-23","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Digital Diagnostics","portco_name":"Digital Diagnostics","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Cedar Pine","Kinderhook","8VC","Optum Ventures","OSF Ventures","Gundersen Health System"],"seller":null,"round":"Series B","stake_pct":null,"amount":75000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Digital Diagnostics Closes $75 million Series B Funding Round led by KKR","summary":"AI diagnostics company Digital Diagnostics closed a $75 million Series B led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=21f72be4-3505-464f-acc2-e36265132059","evidence":"CORALVILLE, Iowa, Aug. 23, 2022 /PRNewswire/ -- Digital Diagnostics, a leading artificial intelligence diagnostic health care technology company, today announced that it has successfully closed a $75 million Series B funding round. Global investment firm KKR led the round, with participation from new and existing investors, including Cedar Pine, Kinderhook, 8VC, Optum Ventures, OSF Ventures, Gundersen Health System, Edward - Elmhurst Health Venture Capital, and the University of Iowa.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:0ab2990af634a5989dbd4f48551345a6","date":"2022-01-12","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Bowery Farming","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":150000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"debt","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Bowery Farming Secures $150 Million Credit Facility Led by KKR to Accelerate Growth","summary":"Vertical farming company Bowery Farming secured a $150 million credit facility led by KKR private credit accounts.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=fbe29acc-ad5d-4552-a358-dbfb5b1a5993","evidence":"NEW YORK, Jan. 12, 2022 /PRNewswire/ -- Bowery Farming (\"Bowery\" or \"the Company\"), the largest vertical farming company in the United States, today announced it has secured a $150 million credit facility led by private credit accounts managed by KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:39faff4b398c4ef9960d0a9858ce7ac9","date":"2021-07-16","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"ON*NET Fibra Colombia","portco_name":"ON*NET Fibra Colombia","target_website":"onnetfibra.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Telefónica","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Telefónica to Create Colombia’s First Nationwide Open Access Fiber Optic Network","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in Telefónica's Colombian fiber network to create an open access company, in a transaction valued at about $500 million, with Telefónica keeping 40%.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=78558ad3-fb05-4263-8909-7a8ee556c77e","evidence":"KKR’s large direct investment in Colombia with a transaction value of approximately $500 million affirms its long-term commitment to the region. As part of the agreement, KKR will acquire a majority stake in Telefónica's existing fiber optic network, the largest in Colombia, and make the network open access through a newly established independent entity, which KKR will control as the majority shareholder. Telefónica will be a minority shareholder in the new company, with a 40% stake.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:57d704bc3059ac79a9e45eff67b6bc2c","date":"2024-05-21","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Vitesse","portco_name":"Vitesse","target_website":"vitesse.io","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Hannover Digital Investments"],"seller":null,"round":"Series C","stake_pct":null,"amount":93000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Vitesse Secures $93M in Series C Funding Led by KKR, Appoints Curt Hess as US Executive President","summary":"Insurance payments platform Vitesse completed a $93 million Series C led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=dc882978-7e89-48a4-accd-be1b475445d4","evidence":"Vitesse, a leading treasury and payment solutions provider for the insurance industry, today announced the completion of a $93M Series C funding round led by leading global investment firm, KKR, with participation from existing investors, including Hannover Digital Investments.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:75142d3a195607c5d9c4912458582312","date":"2020-06-16","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Vinhomes","portco_name":"Vinhomes","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Temasek"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":6.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR-Led Consortium Enters Into a US$650 Million Investment in Vinhomes, a Vingroup Subsidiary That Engages Primarily in Real Estate Development","summary":"A KKR-led consortium including Temasek acquired a c.6% minority stake in Vietnamese developer Vinhomes for VND15.1 trillion (US$650 million).","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4b1190d4-eaba-463d-83c0-b76c4cd33167","evidence":"A KKR-led consortium that includes Temasek has acquired a minority equity stake in Vinhomes JSC, for a total consideration of VND15.1 trillion (US$650 million). The KKR-led consortium has collectively invested VND15.1 trillion (US$650 million) which translates into a c.6% equity stake in Vinhomes.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:9a0872a7efed751d5b70f5754101acd3","date":"2018-01-09","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Blue Sprig","portco_name":"Blue Sprig","target_website":"bluesprigpediatrics.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Forms Blue Sprig Pediatrics to Address Unmet Clinical Needs of Children Diagnosed with Autism","summary":"KKR created autism therapy clinic platform Blue Sprig Pediatrics, funded through its Health Care Strategic Growth Fund.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=927bff92-74f9-4cc8-991d-e7c42a045f5a","evidence":"HOUSTON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR today announced the creation of Blue Sprig Pediatrics, Inc. (“Blue Sprig” or the “Company”), a platform of clinics providing Applied Behavior Analysis (“ABA”) for children diagnosed with Autism Spectrum Disorder (“ASD”). For KKR, the investment is being funded through KKR’s Health Care Strategic Growth Fund, which is focused on investing in high-growth health care-related companies for which KKR can be a unique partner in helping reach scale.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:e125de3b9db90bbe12b4804dbe44a491","date":"2019-05-08","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"MYOB","portco_name":"MYOB","target_website":"myob.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Completes Acquisition of MYOB","summary":"KKR completed its previously announced acquisition of Australian business software company MYOB Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=80b19f37-e961-4a02-a2a2-652bab8aa29f","evidence":"SYDNEY--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Global investment firm KKR and leading Australian online business management company MYOB Group Limited (“MYOB” or the “Company”) today announced the completion of the previously announced acquisition of MYOB by KKR.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:f7413c61f24c11aae5216a546fa26e2a","date":"2022-04-28","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"LOGISTEED","portco_name":"LOGISTEED","target_website":"logisteed.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Hitachi, Ltd.","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Announces Tender Offer to Acquire Hitachi Transport System","summary":"KKR announced a tender offer for Hitachi Transport System (now LOGISTEED) at JPY8,913 per share, with a share buyback from Hitachi at JPY6,632 per share.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=0197fac3-96df-4b91-9800-acbf9d626ac6","evidence":"KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced it intends to make a tender offer for the common shares of Hitachi Transport System Ltd. (“HTS” or the “Company”; TSE stock code 9086) through HTSK Co., Ltd. (the “Offeror”), an entity owned by the investment funds managed by KKR. The proposed tender offer price of JPY8,913 per share and the share buyback price of JPY6,632 per share have been determined based on the negotiations among KKR, HTS, and Hitachi.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7c5eb0bfcd7deb03b7f44710bc7e25bd","date":"2022-10-17","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Treeline Biosciences","portco_name":"Treeline Biosciences","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Rock Springs Capital","ARCH Venture Partners","GV","OrbiMed","Access Industries","T. Rowe Price Associates, Inc.","Ajax Health/Zeus","Casdin Capital","Aisling Capital"],"seller":null,"round":"Series A","stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Treeline Biosciences: An update from our founders","summary":"Treeline Biosciences' founders reported a new financing in which KKR led an expansion of the investor syndicate with a significant commitment from its Health Care Strategic Growth Fund II.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ef512acc-97e0-4e33-8921-bcb267c6a08d","evidence":"Nevertheless, a new and exciting financing deserves mention. KKR has led an expansion of our existing investor syndicate, with a significant capital commitment from its Health Care Strategic Growth Fund II, a fund dedicated to investing in high-growth health care-related companies to which KKR can be a unique and strategic partner in helping reach scale. Other investors in the Series A round included Rock Springs Capital, ARCH Venture Partners, GV, OrbiMed, Access Industries, funds and accounts advised by T. Rowe Price Associates, Inc., Ajax Health/Zeus, Casdin Capital and Aisling Capital.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7bdfc6315d70b695812469cd76ae90cb","date":"2015-12-23","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Joulon","portco_name":"Joulon","target_website":"joulon.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Create Leading Oil and Gas Services Platform","summary":"KKR agreed to establish an integrated oil and gas asset management services platform led by Deepak Munganahalli (later Joulon).","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=c43b706a-af6d-43aa-a459-85dfec770bcf","evidence":"DUBAI, United Arab Emirates & SINGAPORE--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR today announced an agreement to pursue acquisitions and investment opportunities by establishing an integrated entity to provide asset management services to the oil and gas industry globally. The platform will be led by Founder and Executive Chairman Deepak Munganahalli, who brings more than 20 years of global oil and gas experience to the company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:12a31a0f7723d764c93115ddcba6f42e","date":"2015-10-12","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Selecta","portco_name":"Selecta","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Allianz Capital Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR agrees to acquire majority stake in Selecta from ACP","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire Allianz Capital Partners' majority stake in European vending and coffee services company Selecta.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=4482bb3d-1c6a-4e6e-9374-d1619e865365","evidence":"CHAM, Switzerland & LONDON & MUNICH--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced today the signing of a definitive agreement with Allianz Capital Partners (“ACP”) to acquire their majority stake in Selecta Group (“Selecta”). The transaction is subject to, among other things, the consent of Selecta’s bondholders.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:8f963a3e6e5580963c1c0419a27a9fbb","date":"2015-12-08","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"LGC","portco_name":"LGC","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Bridgepoint","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR partners with LGC to facilitate future expansion and growth","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire life sciences measurement and testing company LGC from Bridgepoint for an undisclosed amount.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=554ba813-d63e-4439-a0f3-dff0935e656a","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR today announced that it has agreed to acquire LGC, the international life sciences measurement and testing company, from its current owners Bridgepoint, for an undisclosed amount.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:fc57fd7dc93a66fd250a917445ebc7d0","date":"2015-11-27","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Webhelp","portco_name":"Webhelp","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Charterhouse Capital Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"The management team of Webhelp partners with KKR","summary":"Webhelp's management agreed a partnership with KKR as new investor, becoming controlling shareholders alongside KKR as Charterhouse stepped back.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2135de83-5ec4-4acb-9ba2-e066ffe57d80","evidence":"27 November 2015 - Webhelp, the global business process management and outsourcing solutions group, announced today that it has entered into an agreement with KKR, a leading global investment firm, as new investor and financial partner. The Webhelp management team will now become controlling shareholders, alongside KKR, while Charterhouse Capital Partners will step back after over four years of successful collaboration with the company.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:653814e91db1afcf87af6a7c99ce1643","date":"2015-11-16","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Yuehai Feed Group","portco_name":"Yuehai Feed Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Completes Investment in Yuehai Feed Group","summary":"KKR completed an investment in Chinese aquatic feed company Yuehai Feed Group.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f4242224-d20d-4d94-8c9b-87cc16a773e2","evidence":"GUANGDONG, China--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR has completed an investment in Yuehai Feed Group Co. Ltd. (“Yuehai” or the “Company”), a leading aquatic feed company in China focused on providing feed and nutrition solutions for shrimp and seawater fish farming.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b30f3a88b70e9c637fce73193705e647","date":"2015-11-17","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Avendus Capital","portco_name":"Avendus Capital","target_website":"avendus.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in Avendus Capital to Build a Next Generation Multi-Asset Financial Services Platform","summary":"KKR agreed to invest in Indian financial services firm Avendus Capital from its Asian Fund II to fund its credit, wealth and alternatives businesses.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=deb6b868-4a63-4f90-98b1-d72531712b75","evidence":"MUMBAI, India--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Leading global investment firm KKR and Avendus Capital (“Avendus” or “the Company”), a pre-eminent Indian financial services firm providing customized solutions in the areas of financial advisory and wealth management, today announced the signing of a definitive agreement under which KKR will invest in Avendus to fund the company’s foray into the credit solutions business and to grow its wealth and alternative asset management solutions offerings to its customers. KKR is making its investment from its Asian Fund II.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4c1e27e990511f3563be9d1a171bb3c5","date":"2015-11-17","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"SoftwareONE","portco_name":"SoftwareONE","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":25.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"SoftwareONE partners with KKR to accelerate future growth","summary":"KKR closed its growth capital investment in SoftwareONE, acquiring a 25% stake.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=da0417d0-e5e2-43d8-9313-5cedce2bb4b3","evidence":"STANS, Switzerland & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- SoftwareONE, one of the leading global providers of software portfolio management solutions and KKR, a leading global investment firm, announced today the closing of the transaction, announced on 17 August 2015. KKR provides growth capital and acquires a 25% stake position in SoftwareONE.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7164985a4fbbbd8f93ab120900c7a066","date":"2015-11-16","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"EchoNous","portco_name":"EchoNous","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":35000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Signostics Announces Investment and Capital Partnership with KKR","summary":"Handheld ultrasound developer Signostics (later EchoNous) announced a $35 million private investment from KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=720b13a8-55b4-4682-8f60-39b7ba097a64","evidence":"CLOVELLY PARK, Australia--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Signostics, a start-up innovator in the field of highly miniaturized ultrasound technology, today announced a private investment of $35 million dollars from KKR, a leading global investment firm.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:3b6f1a9c1c17d6d45920c8467e226293","date":"2015-11-13","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"GetYourGuide","portco_name":"GetYourGuide","target_website":"getyourguide.com","investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Spark Capital","Highland Capital Partners","Sunstone Capital","Nokia Growth Partners"],"seller":null,"round":"growth","stake_pct":null,"amount":50000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"GetYourGuide Raises $50 Million Growth Round Led By KKR","summary":"KKR led a $50 million growth equity round in Berlin travel activities marketplace GetYourGuide.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=1f76b325-ba1f-488e-add6-c66df6c14346","evidence":"BERLIN & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that it is leading a $50 million growth equity investment in Berlin-based GetYourGuide, the leading independent online marketplace for discovering and booking travel activities worldwide. The company’s existing investors, Spark Capital, Highland Capital Partners and Sunstone Capital as well as new investor Nokia Growth Partners (NGP) will join KKR in its round of financing.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:04b8593f63789691269a35edc41d86ca","date":"2015-11-02","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"CA Media","portco_name":"CA Media","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["The Chernin Group"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and The Chernin Group’s CA Media Announce Partnership","summary":"KKR and The Chernin Group's CA Media formed a partnership including the creation of Asian media investment vehicle Emerald Media.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=2307660b-2633-4c9c-9792-7fb6259cb918","evidence":"MUMBAI, HONG KONG & SINGAPORE--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Global investment firm KKR and The Chernin Group, LLC today announced a multi-faceted partnership that includes the creation of Emerald Media, a new vehicle to fund investments capitalizing on fast-growing opportunities in the media and entertainment industries across Asia.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:57f70ed74f5a7ef81f946d2c3a82e191","date":"2015-10-22","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Cohera Medical","portco_name":"Cohera Medical","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":50000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cohera Medical, Inc.® Announces $50 Million in New Financing","summary":"Surgical adhesives developer Cohera Medical closed the first tranche of a $50 million equity financing led by KKR.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=b2007ae5-73ca-4469-9793-932ef0f78e16","evidence":"PITTSBURGH--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Cohera Medical, a leading innovator and developer of absorbable surgical adhesives and sealants, announced closing the first tranche of a $50 million equity financing led by KKR, a leading global investment firm, with participation from existing private investors.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:e5bcf3b1a1030443651fc679c2a65a4a","date":"2015-10-13","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"58 Home","portco_name":"58 Home","target_website":null,"investor":"Alibaba Group Holding Limited","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["KKR","Ping An Group"],"seller":null,"round":"Series A","stake_pct":null,"amount":300000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":1000000000.0,"valuation_currency":"USD","headline":"58.com Subsidiary 58 Home Raises US$300 million with Participation from KKR","summary":"58.com's 58 Home subsidiary signed a US$300 million Series A with Alibaba, KKR and Ping An, valuing it at over US$1 billion post-investment.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=24bbf065-028b-4bc7-88be-33fa5a5f313b","evidence":"BEIJING, China, October 12, 2015/PRNewswire - 58.com Inc. (NYSE: WUBA) (collectively with its subsidiaries and other consolidated entities, “58.com”), China’s largest online marketplace offering multi-category local services, today announced the signing of a definitive shares subscription agreement (“SPA”) for a US$300 million Series A equity funding round for 58 Daojia Inc., the 58 Home subsidiary of 58.com, with participation from Alibaba Group Holding Limited (“Alibaba”), global investment firm KKR and Ping An Group (“Ping An”). With the proceeds from this equity funding, which values 58 Home at over US$1 billion on a fully-diluted basis post-investment, 58 Home intends to continue to enhance the platform with further investments in marketing, research and development, and other operating initiatives.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:77fe980c84dff387228d86c77a09f851","date":"2015-09-22","date_text":null,"kind":"other","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Trans European Oil & Gas","portco_name":"Trans European Oil & Gas","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Backs Highly Experienced E&P Team to Launch Trans European Oil & Gas","summary":"KKR agreed to back the former Star Energy management team to launch European oil and gas company Trans European Oil & Gas.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=d9337cc6-02ae-4bbd-a412-1185899c3a98","evidence":"LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that it will back Roland Wessel, Colin Judd and Melvyn Horgan, founders and former management team of Star Energy, to launch Trans European Oil & Gas Limited (“Trans European Oil & Gas”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:90fb3338a05d1bf61d45148d3f558b78","date":"2015-09-10","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"Optimal+","portco_name":"Optimal+","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Carmel Ventures","Pitango"],"seller":null,"round":"growth","stake_pct":null,"amount":42000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"round_size","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Optimal+ Raises $42 Million Growth Round Led By KKR","summary":"KKR led a $42 million growth equity investment in semiconductor big data analytics company Optimal+.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=ba7991c0-80b5-469e-bc40-0a3127aae0d6","evidence":"LONDON & TEL AVIV, Israel--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, today announced that it is leading a $42 million growth equity investment in Optimal+, a big data analytics company that provides highly actionable insights to the semiconductor industry. KKR makes its investment alongside the existing lead investors Carmel Ventures and Pitango, two of Israel’s most preeminent venture capital funds.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:8e117888e8862ca6ee7d021a842a64a1","date":"2015-07-31","date_text":null,"kind":"minority_investment","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"JBF Group","portco_name":"JBF Group","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":20.0,"amount":150000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"stake_price","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Invests in India’s JBF Group","summary":"KKR agreed to invest US$150 million into JBF Group, including acquiring a 20% stake in listed JBF Industries.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=8ca9275c-1c5e-4834-b75d-74c1c355811a","evidence":"MUMBAI, India--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- JBF Industries Ltd. (“JBF”), a leading manufacturer of polyester value-chain products, has signed a definitive agreement with global investment firm KKR under which KKR will invest US$150 million into JBF Group, an entity that includes JBF’s international subsidiaries. A portion of the proceeds will be used by KKR to acquire a 20% stake in JBF, listed on the BSE Ltd. and National Stock Exchange of India.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:ee8b02b6539c0b53110a76d519d09a11","date":"2015-07-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Hanseatic Ship Asset Management","portco_name":"Hanseatic Ship Asset Management","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Borealis Maritime"],"seller":"Commerzbank AG","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":254500000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Borealis Maritime Joint Venture Acquires Large Fleet from Commerzbank","summary":"A KKR and Borealis Maritime joint venture acquired Commerzbank's ship asset manager HSAM and its 18-vessel fleet for $254.5 million.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=7a703f3a-4c63-46fa-afcb-4e4b4e82541c","evidence":"HAMBURG, Germany--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR and Borealis Maritime today announced the $254.5 million acquisition of Hanseatic Ship Asset Management GmbH, a 100 percent owned subsidiary of Commerzbank AG controlling a modern fleet of 18 container and dry cargo vessels, through a joint venture vehicle established by the two firms.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:3f969110e7ba5396993c632aa1bb1d08","date":"2015-07-21","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"X-ELIO","portco_name":"X-ELIO","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Gestamp Renewables","round":null,"stake_pct":80.0,"amount":1000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR Acquires an 80% Stake in Gestamp Solar","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire an 80% stake in Gestamp Solar (later X-ELIO) from Gestamp Renewables in a deal valuing it at a total enterprise value of around $1 billion.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=f9e68f69-5c05-4937-ab5f-0c0037cd78a3","evidence":"MADRID & LONDON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR a leading global investor, has reached a definitive agreement to acquire from Gestamp Renewables an 80% stake in Gestamp Asetym Solar, S.L. (“Gestamp Solar”), a premier global solar PV developer and operator. The transaction values Gestamp Solar at a total enterprise value of around $1 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:34177cfc54a1f1f226573e3f23d7419e","date":"2015-07-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Deutsche Glasfaser","portco_name":"Deutsche Glasfaser","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Reggeborgh","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR and Reggeborgh Announce Partnership For Strong Expansion Of Deutsche Glasfaser","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire a majority stake in German fibre network operator Deutsche Glasfaser from Reggeborgh, with about €450m earmarked for roll-out.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=81dcbab8-fff5-4b80-b775-8d437b5c6153","evidence":"LONDON & RIJSSEN, Netherlands & BORKEN, Germany--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- KKR, a leading global investment firm, and Reggeborgh (“RB”), a leading Dutch investment firm, today announced a partnership for the strong expansion of Deutsche Glasfaser (“DG”). KKR will acquire a majority stake in DG, which is currently fully owned by Reggeborgh. In a joint effort, the two partners will provide DG with the long-term capital to embark on an ambitious growth program whereby approximately €450m is to be invested in the further roll-out of the German fibre optics infrastructure over the next few years.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:af7bfa7fa97ec0944a0402783c39fde6","date":"2015-06-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Capital Safety","portco_name":"Capital Safety","target_website":null,"investor":"3M","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"KKR","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2500000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"3M to Acquire Capital Safety","summary":"3M agreed to acquire fall protection maker Capital Safety from KKR for a total enterprise value of $2.5 billion including about $0.7 billion of debt.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=9782fe46-1be2-4731-b3cd-2d3b79e0f90e","evidence":"ST. PAUL, Minn.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- 3M announced today that it has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Capital Safety from KKR for a total enterprise value of $2.5 billion, including the assumption of approximately $0.7 billionof debt, net of cash acquired.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:71a8a0ddfc6b4aa32763d533219f2fcd","date":"2015-06-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"C.H.I. Overhead Doors","portco_name":"C.H.I. Overhead Doors","target_website":null,"investor":"KKR","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"FFL","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"KKR to Acquire C.H.I. Overhead Doors from FFL","summary":"KKR agreed to acquire garage door maker C.H.I. Overhead Doors from FFL; terms undisclosed.","source_name":"KKR","source_url":"https://media.kkr.com/news-details/?news_id=335c2177-478a-4b3c-af33-94b0a2a0c5c5","evidence":"NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- C.H.I. Overhead Doors (“CHI”), a North American manufacturer of residential and commercial garage doors, announced today that KKR, a leading global investment firm, is acquiring the company from FFL, a San Francisco-based middle-market private equity firm. Terms of the transaction were not disclosed.","verifi